INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2217, 254, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'label_add', '2026-10-19 19:48:47.586855+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"id": 7, "value": "qibla"}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2218, 230, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.828821+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "PR: https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/50581\n\nMonitoring row for PR `expo/expo#50581`, which makes the background network requirement configurable. The local patch `patches/expo-background-task+58.0.11.patch` adds `requiresNetworkConnectivity` to `BackgroundTaskOptions` (default true); the app registers with `false` (`stores/notifications.ts`) so the notification refresh runs offline, and published builds to 58.0.11 hardcode both constraints. The patch dies at the first re-pin past the release. Competing draft `expo/expo#48469` stalled since 2026-08-04; issue #48122 carries a needs review label. Carries the retired issue ledger''s item 37. Opened 2026-10-09, open and unmerged at the 2026-10-17 re-check."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2222, 3, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.917802+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "PR: https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/51291\n\nMonitoring row for the `expo-location` compass corrections. Three corrections to `expo-location`''s own code, so Expo maintains them and this repo carries nothing once merged and released: iOS `headingFilter` is never set (on the XS, 731 of 731 readings were discarded); the Android 2-degree emission gate starves a slow turn (0.83 Hz at 2 degrees per second), so it becomes configurable; `headingAccuracy` is bucketed 0 to 3 and the negative invalid-heading sentinel collapses into bucket 0, so it goes numeric. The local patch `patches/expo-location+58.0.17.patch` (Android 50Hz sensors, no emission gate, module from source; iOS `kCLHeadingFilterNone`) dies at the first re-pin past the release, proven on a phone per the standing re-pin rule. Waiting on Expo reviewing and releasing."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2223, 233, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.939734+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "Recorded by ticket 143 on the owner''s order. When a published `expo-widgets` release carries `__expoWidgetDeviceLocale`, this row deletes the local patch''s device-locale hunks (`patches/expo-widgets+58.0.20.patch`), records the shipped state on the board (the tracking rows are #239 and #232), and re-proves the widget faces on a phone at that re-pin. Do nothing before the release exists."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2225, 4, 'comment', 'owner', 'Re-scoped 2026-10-19 by the owner''s rulings: the patch half belongs to the upstream rows, the qibla copy is confirmed fine on glass, the hygiene pass stays and this row is worked last. The stale file references are gone from the description; the record lives in git history.', NULL, '2026-10-19 19:49:05.977653+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2219, 231, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.85015+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "PR: https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/51290\n\nMonitoring row for PR `expo/expo#51290`: the Android Glance converter drops the `fillMaxWidth` fraction (a 0.5 renders at 1.0) and has no `weight` case. This is the true cause behind row 15d''s proportional-layout workaround; nothing in this repo changes until it merges, and the workaround simplifies only at the owner''s say. Removes no patch."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2220, 232, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.872571+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "PR: https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/51292\n\nMonitoring row for PR `expo/expo#51292`, which adds the `openApp` option to the Android widget `Button`. Every Android card state wraps itself in it (`widgets/PrayerWidget.tsx`); without it a tap does nothing. WidgetKit opens on tap by platform default, so iOS never depends on this half. At the first re-pin past its release the openApp half of `patches/expo-widgets+58.0.20.patch` dies."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2221, 239, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.893993+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "PR: https://github.com/expo/expo/pull/51793\n\nMonitoring row for PR `expo/expo#51793`, filed 2026-10-19 from this repo: it exposes the device locale to widget JS runtimes through a `__expoWidgetDeviceLocale` global. The local patch''s device-locale half feeds the neutral, stale and catch faces (the D44/D79 device-keyed statics); without it those faces lose their locale. When a published release carries the global, board row #233 deletes the local patch''s device-locale hunks and this row closes."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2226, 4, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'title', '2026-10-19 19:49:35.278837+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "Final hygiene pass: a deep review and cleanup of code and board"}, "from": {"value": "Patches, one line of qibla copy, repository hygiene"}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2227, 4, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:35.278837+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "Goal: the last row on the board - a deep review and cleanup of the codebase (typing, dead code, pattern drift) and the board, so both end clean.\n\nWhere: the whole repository and the open board.\n\nTHE ORDER OF THIS ROW (owner, 2026-10-19): picked LAST, after every other row is Done or parked. The number-order picking rule yields to this order.\n\nCLOSED 2026-10-19 by the owner''s rulings: the one line of qibla copy verified on glass (the sheet''s subheading reads right); the one leftover build covered by the owner''s full-app test on the 3T, which works perfectly; the patch questions owned by the upstream rows; the 2026-10-14 hygiene check (already done) folds into this broader pass.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] every other board row Done or parked\n- [ ] a deep typed code review run across the repo, findings fixed or ticketed\n- [ ] dead code, stale comments and pattern drift cleaned\n- [ ] the board swept: no defect the integrity checklist can catch\n- [ ] yarn validate green at the close"}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2224, 4, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 19:49:05.960805+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "Goal: close the 2026-10-14 bundle''s remainder - one verification question and the repository hygiene pass.\n\nWhere: the 3T, the repo.\n\nThe bundle''s other parts are closed or superseded (owner''s rulings 2026-10-19): the patch questions are the board''s upstream rows (#51 #230 #231 #232 #239) under the standing rule that every patch is re-proven at each re-pin; the one line of qibla copy is merged and the owner read it fine on glass; the hygiene pass stays and this row is worked last among the current Backlog rows.\n\nLEFT from the original bundle: one build (the one without the Android hunks) was never made because the owner lacked the 3T. The 2026-10-17 SDK 58 re-pin regenerated every patch whole and proved them on phones, so the planner''s first check is whether that covers the leftover; if it does, this row closes by verification.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] the leftover''s purpose verified against the 2026-10-17 re-pin record: covered, or one build and one read on the 3T\n- [ ] the hygiene pass run once\n- [ ] no patch or upstream work: those live on the board''s rows"}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2228, 4, 'comment', 'owner', 'Re-scoped 2026-10-19 by the owner: the qibla copy verified on glass (''Hold flat and turn slowly'' reads right on the sheet), the leftover 3T build covered by the owner''s full-app test on the 3T, and this row becomes the board''s last ticket - a deep typed review and cleanup of code and board, picked only after every other row is done.', NULL, '2026-10-19 19:49:35.300345+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
