INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2527, 271, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 2 measured on the two simulators, build 2.1.35 Release (mock data drives the schedule; geometry is the subject).

Duo open pose, landscape (SIMULATOR_UDID, iOS 27.1): launched fresh in the open pose, the window spans the lit panel at 951x669 - the hierarchy reads the application frame as the full panel. The gradient runs edge to edge: a pixel scan of the middle row found zero pure-black side pixels where row 264 measured 241pt bars each side (re-measured this session: that old letterbox state still reads bars at x=0-240 and x=710-950), and the spanning frame reads the gradient''s own navy at x=0 rising to violet at x=950, with one bezel pixel at the top-right corner and nothing else. The countdown and schedule sit centred: the countdown block and the whole 500pt content column start at x=225.7, about 225pt margins either side. The honored top inset reads 0 (the countdown block sits at y=23) and the bottom chrome sits 34pt above the bottom edge. The attached image is this frame.

Duo open pose, portrait hold: this window class could not be produced. Both portrait rotation asks left the spanning landscape window untouched, and a relaunch under a portrait ask still came up spanning landscape; the plan''s expected 669x951 spanning portrait class never appeared on this simulator. The only portrait presentation observed on the inner panel was the old compat-scaled 469x669 letterbox, reached by unfolding a process that had launched folded - and that window keeps its honored top inset at 0 too, the 2.1.24 clamp eating the scaled window''s phantom, exactly the pre-change presentation the ruling removes.

Duo half-open: asked from the closed pose, the inner panel lit with the same spanning 951x669 class - no scaled 469x669 window, no push-down of the countdown (block at y=23, matching the open pose). The hinge angle could not be read back on this simulator, so half-open and open glass cannot be distinguished with these instruments; the window-class reading itself stands.

Duo closed pose: a landscape rotation ask was refused - the window stayed 466x678 portrait after the ask, same process.

Open-closed-open round trip: one live process throughout (pid 18279 at every checkpoint), the closed legs rendering 466x678 and the open legs rendering the spanning 951x669 each time. Notably the unfold of a process that launched folded still hands back the letterboxed 469x669 window rather than spanning, until the next relaunch - the plan''s recorded re-ask risk family, not chased here.

Clamp verdict: no open-pose reading exceeds 62 - every spanning read shows the countdown at y=23 (honored top 0) with phone-class bottom chrome (34pt). Clamp identity, no code change; Decision 5''s park condition did not fire.

Phone-class witness (iPhone 18 Pro, iOS 27.0): rotation asks in both landscape directions were refused - the window stayed 402x874 portrait through both asks, same process, no reflow.', NULL, '2026-10-20 03:55:41.247101+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
