INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2639, 276, 'comment', 'owner', 'VERDICT: PASS (blind review of a84a70e1, uat..lane/276b)

The restructure is correct and its tests are real pins, but two consequences outside the suite need carrying:

1. minor: e2e/device-atlas-sm-s911b.md:43 records the Settings button at (540, 2122), e2e/flows/sheets-x10.yaml:7 taps (540,1730) and e2e/flows/language-switch-x1.yaml:7 taps (540,1830) - all measured on the old layout. This commit moves the button down 25 CSS px (the wrapper''s bottom: SIZE.nav.bottomOffset = 25 above the dots-anchor collapses to the button''s bottom edge sitting AT that anchor), which is beyond the button''s HIT_SLOP.lg of 15 (shared/constants.ts:651), so the next replay of those flows taps dead space above the button. Nothing under e2e/ was re-measured. Re-measure on each atlas phone and write the y back.

2. minor: app/Navigation.tsx:104 - the new bar container keeps default pointerEvents (''auto''), so its now-contiguous footprint (dot + 8px gap + button + 8px gap + dot, full button height, all on one line at the anchor) swallows pager swipes in the gaps and the dots band, where the old disjoint layout (a 20x6 dots strip plus the button 25px higher) let them through. chromeLayer already models the fix with pointerEvents={''box-none''} at app/Navigation.tsx:72; the bar wants the same (and ''none'' on the decorative dots).

Confirmations checked:

3. Suite verified: npx jest __tests__/app/Navigation.test.tsx --selectProjects=components in the lane worktree - 18/18 pass, 3.1s.

4. Test quality: the four-cell anchor table pins both platform arms and the max clamp (ios 0 -> SPACING.xl, ios 34 -> 34, android 0 -> SPACING.md, android 10 -> inset + md); the children-order test pins dot-button-dot exactly; row/center/gap styles, per-dot a11y hiding, and the no-wrapper parent link are each pinned. Swapping the ternary arms or uncentering the row fails these tests as claimed; not trivia.

5. Z-order intact: the deleted wrapper zIndex was a duplicate - the button''s own styles.container still carries zIndex: 0 with the "never appear above sheets or overlays" comment (components/ui/SettingsButton.tsx:49); Overlay renders after Navigation (app/index.tsx:276-277) so it paints above the bar; sheets are portal-presented BottomSheetModals.

6. Chrome fade, launch defer, first-frame settled: unchanged wiring - chromeOpacityStyle still fades the whole bar with the overlay, the bar was never chromeDeferred (nor were the dots before), dot/button opacities are state-derived settled values, and the button''s press scale starts at 1. No entering animation was introduced.

7. RTL: the row mirrors under layout direction exactly as the old dots row did; no new directional assumption (no start/end, centring via alignSelf).

8. Dead code: SIZE.nav.bottomOffset and the dotsContainer/dotsRow/buttonWrapper styles are fully gone with zero remaining references (grep across ts/tsx/kt/swift/sh/yaml).

9. Commit discipline: one commit; 2.1.33 -> 2.2.0 in package.json and app.json together, minor for the feat-typed subject, matching prior bumps (android build.gradle is gitignored and prebuild-generated from app.json); author pseudonym Athan preserved; no secrets, device identifiers or screenshots in the diff (the 390x844 frame is the library''s doc-example metrics, not a device fingerprint); scope is tight - constants.ts loses only the dead nav block.', NULL, '2026-10-20 05:56:56.072216+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2640, 276, 'comment', 'owner', 'PLAN-CONFORMANCE AUDIT (a84a70e1, uat..lane/276b): PASS

1. minor: e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md line 56 (Settings button ~ (540, 1830)) and the Settings taps in sheets-x10, sounds-x5, toggles-x10 (540,1730) and language-switch-x1 (540,1830) were recorded against the old position; this commit moves the button down exactly 25dp (the deleted SIZE.nav.bottomOffset wrapper offset), so by the atlas''s own rule (change the screen state and the numbers are void) they are stale. At the 3T''s stock density the taps still land (1730 now rides the 15dp hitSlop margin, 1830 the button skin), so nothing is broken today, but the Step 4 / Android-read follow-up this row already tables must re-measure and write that row and the 1730 taps back; nothing on the row yet records the drift.

Confirmations checked:
2. Design 1 geometry holds: one row (flexDirection row, alignItems center, gap 8) of dot, Settings button, dot; the anchor expression is byte-identical to uat''s, so the button''s bottom edge sits on today''s dots-bottom line, clear of the home indicator, the button being the tallest centred child; the column, wrapper and dots-row are gone and the footprint is the single line.
3. Nothing else moves: the only code hunk is the bar block and its styles; countdown, lists, sheets, pager and the dot style bytes are untouched.
4. First-frame settled: no animation added or retimed; the dots keep their value-only opacity animation and the bar keeps the chrome fade.
5. The nine cancelled variants and the debug switcher stay dead: a tree-wide grep finds no switcher, no env flag, no wrapper or SIZE.nav reference; the branch is exactly one commit over uat.
6. Shared UI: one layout in app/Navigation.tsx, the platform split confined to the anchor value; both arms tested (ios 0 and 34, android 0 and 10).
7. Gates: I ran yarn validate in the worktree, exit 0, 227 suites and 5879 tests green, coverage 100 percent on statements, branches, functions and lines, which covers every changed line; red-before-green holds by construction (the suite''s testIDs and row assertions cannot pass against the merge-base) and both claimed mutations provably break a named assertion (ios inset 0 expects 20, the swapped arm yields 12; an uncentred row fails the style assertion).
8. Version discipline: one commit, package.json and app.json move 2.1.33 to 2.2.0 together, minor on a feat subject with the patch reset; android/app/build.gradle is untracked prebuild output, so the two tracked surfaces are both bumped.
9. Hygiene: five text files only, no screenshot or binary, no UDID, serial or device name anywhere in the commit, author and committer both the pseudonym.

Row items still open by design, not diff defects: the Step 4 iPhone XS verification, the shipped screenshot, the designs 2-10 attachment cleanup, then the merge with the board snapshot.', NULL, '2026-10-20 05:58:36.56858+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
