INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2643, 276, 'comment', 'owner', 'Both reviews passed (comments 2639 and 2640). Adjudication: the confirmed hit-testing finding - the bar''s contiguous band eating pager swipes over the gaps and dots - is fixed at 2.2.1, red before green with mutation evidence, validate green at full coverage. The stale-coordinate finding both reviews raised is recorded, not code-fixed: the button moved down 25 and every recorded tap still lands (the 1730 taps ride the 15dp slop with about 10px to spare, the 1830 taps the button skin), but by the atlas''s own rule the records are void - the atlas rows and flow comments (S911B 540,2122; 3T 540,1830 and the 1730 taps in sheets-x10, sounds-x5, toggles-x10, language-switch) are stale until re-measured, which is tabled with this row''s Android read follow-up since it needs the phones.', NULL, '2026-10-20 06:06:59.154739+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2644, 280, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 1 measured on the Duo simulator (iOS 27.1), today''s build 2.1.34 Release, portrait-only plist (both arrays the portrait pair, no delegate override in the prebuild product).

The instrument: agent-device''s orientation command accepted every value - portrait, portrait-upside-down, landscape-left and landscape-right each replied "Rotated to X" - but the canvas class stayed 469x669, the wide compat letterbox, through all four, on a fresh launch made in the open pose. No value produced the tall 669x951 class. The command is screen-inert on this simulator, not merely app-refused: on the home screen and with the app foregrounded, the panel captures after the portrait ask and after the landscape-right ask are byte-identical (zero pixels differ of 636219). The Device Hub fallback could not be exercised: this host''s Xcode ships no Simulator app, so the Device Hub control surface does not exist, and simctl carries no orientation verb. The tall hold is therefore not producible with the instruments this host has, and no tall-hold screenshot exists.

Today''s build read in the producible hold (open, landscape, second launch after install): the window sits in the 469x669 compat class on the 951x669 panel, letterboxed - the middle-row pixel scan reads pure-black bars across x 0 to 240 and x 710 to 950, the gradient confined between, matching row 264''s record. The app exposes no inset reading in Release, so the snapshot geometry stands as the record: the countdown name text at y=13, the designed post-clamp offset, so the honored top inset reads 0 (the 2.1.24 clamp eating the scaled window''s phantom ~80), and the deepest visible control bottoms at y=610 of 669.

Live rotate from the landscape hold toward the tall hold under one pid: the portrait ask was accepted, the window class stayed 469x669 wide with the letterbox standing, and the pid survived.

Closed-pose control: the closed fold landed at 466x678 (today''s closed class) under the same pid, the gradient edge to edge with no black bars, and a landscape rotation ask in the closed pose left the window 466x678 portrait - no effect.

The recorded live-unfold limitation carried over unchanged: the throwaway first launch, made while folded, kept its 469x669 letterbox on live unfold until relaunch.

Outcome: rotation refused or ineffective across all four values and the fallback - the tall hold never materialised, so today''s letterboxed presentation is the only reading this host can produce. The row''s Blocked branch (a landed tall pose whose canvas stays wide or letterboxed) did not fire because no tall pose landed; the tall canvas remains unmeasured pending an instrument that can rotate this simulator.', NULL, '2026-10-20 06:14:07.402929+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2592, 276, 'comment', 'owner', 'FINDINGS (plan-conformance): PASS
1. Ten attachments design-01.png through design-10.png sit on the row in upload order, each with its one-line comment naming the arrangement and its trade.
2. Design 1 in DesignSwitcher.tsx renders dot-button-dot on one centred row whose layer sits at anchor = Math.max(insets.bottom, SPACING.xl) on iOS - exactly today''s dots-bottom line, since the in-flow dotsRow alone sizes today''s container - so the button''s bottom edge lands on it with the two real dots flanking left and right.
3. ChromeGate returns Navigation''s own element unless EXPO_PUBLIC_DESIGN_SWITCHER === ''1'', so every build without the env renders today''s chrome through an unchanged host tree.
4. Nothing leaked: both commits touch only seven text files, no screenshot or recording is committed, and the diff and commit messages carry no device identifier (the three device serials this review originally quoted verbatim now stand as their placeholders), no device display name and no person name.
5. Nothing merged: lane/276 appears on no remote and neither commit is reachable from any remote branch; the main tree''s uat still points at e824d0ce with a clean tree.
6. The independent pixel read (badges D1/10..D10/10 in order, arrangements matching, no modals) stands as given; the plan''s tap-only cycling also gained a documented ten-second auto-cycle at 2.1.35, and the plan''s own badge provision is what proves the order held.

(Identifier sweep, 280''s lane: this comment''s fourth point originally quoted three device serials verbatim; they are replaced above per the repository''s public-identifier rule, caught by the identifier gate when the board snapshot regenerated.)', NULL, '2026-10-20 05:18:44.720873+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', '2026-10-20 06:24:45.284+00');
