INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2710, 272, 'comment', 'owner', 'Closed. Wiped from the published history: both owner names, in every commit identity and in every line of every blob and commit message; every store-id spelling, which now arrives from outside the repository at build time; the home-path username, written as $HOME from here on; the Apple team and certificate identifiers; both device identifiers and the phone serial the machine-local list holds; the tool-session scratchpad paths; and the five historical design renders the media rule refuses. Every commit on every ref reads Athan <athan@athan.uk>.

Verified from a fresh clone of origin: the gate''s own tree scan and its full-history scan over 4,944 commits print nothing; an independent pass over all 40,344 objects in that clone finds no manifest term, no entry of the 26-line denylist, no store id, no scratchpad path and no home path; every identity reads Athan; the clone prebuilds as com.example.athan, with the notification receiver under its own package and no EAS project id, so a stranger deploys this as their own. Both owner builds badge the published Android id unchanged at versionCode 1000000 (prod and mock, versionName 2.2.4, the same signer).

Enforcement, all deterministic: the tracked pre-commit hook refuses a staged term and an owner identity, the suite''s tree test inside the pre-push path catches a commit made with hooks off, and board/snapshot.sh refuses a dump that carries a term.

For the record: uat and the board branch pushed through the normal hook path; main''s push needed the repository ruleset lifted (non_fast_forward, required_linear_history, pull_request) and all five rules restored immediately after.

Tabled, not blocking: refs/pull/168/head (dfa06c29) still serves pre-rewrite objects on GitHub and only GitHub support can purge it; the GitHub account handle and the store developer name are name-derived and wait on two separate owner decisions.', NULL, '2026-10-20 08:59:26.560767+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
