INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3153, 322, 'comment', 'owner', 'Planned: plan doc T-322 (id 34) linked to the row, four code steps at 2 points each. The planning note is resolved - both the reset ink and the doubled qibla line are alpha-0 text ink from 294''s conversion, confirmed on uat. Grilling the plan next.', NULL, '2026-10-24 12:26:34.222276+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3154, 322, 'comment', 'owner', 'Owner order (dictated 2026-10-24): after the audit passes and before the row moves to Awaiting Owner, the lead builds a real production compile with the mock data - not a dev build - through the single build slot, installs it on both phones (the 3T and the iPhone XS), and then parks the row. The owner reads the polish items on the production build so the performance and the transitions feel real.', NULL, '2026-10-24 12:40:11.500868+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3155, 322, 'comment', 'owner', 'FINDINGS

1. FATAL - Step 2 ("alpha-0 text ink leaves the tree"), Decision 1, and the acceptance criterion "the text-ink sweep inside yarn validate bans alpha-0 text colour outright". The step''s red-first claim - "watched red, it names exactly the reset''s ''transparent'' and the donor''s ''transparent''" - is false: the tightened sweep names NEITHER site, so the red run cannot be observed and the ban is vacuous. I ran the sweep''s own helpers (copied verbatim from components/__tests__/textInk.test.ts) over all of app/ and components/ with the alpha-0 carve-out dropped: zero offences, with both ''transparent''s standing. Two independent causes: the reset''s ink rides `const resetInk = !isCustomColor ? ''transparent'' : ...` (ColorPicker.tsx:99), and colourConsts (textInk.test.ts:84) binds only whole string/COLORS-path consts, so the inline `{ color: resetInk }` never resolves to a leaf; the donor''s `color: ''transparent''` (Qibla.tsx:263) is preceded by the `// Invisible ink...` comment, and propertyValue''s anchor regex `(?:^|[,{])\s*color\s*:` cannot match across a comment. A control file with a plain uncommented entry IS caught, so this is the sweep''s blindness, not my method. Consequence: the tightened test passes green while both sites keep alpha-0, and a future alpha-0 in either shape passes green too - exactly what the criterion claims cannot happen. Fix: the step must make both sites sweep-visible and say how - inline the reset''s ternary into its style expression (quoted literals are caught directly), and drop or move the donor''s inline comment so `color:` follows its comma directly - or extend colourConsts/propertyValue to resolve ternary consts and strip comments; then restate what the red run actually names.

2. FATAL - Design "The hidden inks", Risk bullet 2 ("Verified today for both sites"), and Step 2''s per-state pin. The claim "verified: no background between either text and the sheet surface" is false for the reset: ColorPicker is hosted inside the settings sheet''s Countdown Bar Card (Settings.tsx:156-166), whose background is rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.06) (Settings.tsx:219) over the sheet - a face of about rgb(16, 29, 69), not COLORS.surface.sheet''s rgb(11, 24, 58). Painting opaque #0b183a glyph ink there renders a visible dark word over a lighter card on BOTH platforms - it would turn the hidden reset into a shown one and regress iPhone, where ''transparent'' already hides correctly. The donor half of the claim holds: the Sheet header carries no background. Fix: the reset''s hidden ink must be the card face flattened to one opaque constant (0.06 of rgba(99,102,241) over #0b183a, the repo''s established flatten pattern), named in the plan and pinned per-state in ColorPicker.test.tsx; narrow the Risk bullet''s "verified" to the donor alone.

Everything else survives hostile reading: both alpha-0 sites and only they exist; renderBackdrop is 0.9 over COLORS.surface.backdrop #000116, and rgba(0, 1, 22, 0.9) is exactly those channels; the modal overlay and both header labels paint what the plan says today (ColorPicker.tsx:263, Countdown.tsx:118, Day.tsx:74); Countdown.test.tsx:189 is the text.secondary pin; overlayProgress and showOverlayDate at ANIMATION.duration exist as ridden; the colour arithmetic checks out (#6c79c2 is h231 s41 l59; #7485b9 is h225 s33 l59; #7173bc is h238 s36 l59; #031a4c is h221, #5b1eaa is h266); useDerivedColor is gone from hooks/useAnimation.ts with its old fromColor/toColor signature recoverable from git, so the sweep''s TEXT_INK_HOOKS guards it on return; all six locales'' help.a.widgets begin with the Latin labels and nothing else does; help.test.ts, Help.test.tsx, DayLines.test.tsx, ColorPicker.test.tsx and Qibla.test.tsx all exist and can carry the claimed pins; uat is 2.4.17 in all four version files; the fetch-origin patch rule matches the repo''s; points and subtasks agree with the ticket; no step touches a device, build or install.', NULL, '2026-10-24 12:42:56.187151+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3156, 324, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-24 12:46:24.526588+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "The text-ink sweep drops its 0 carve-out on every arm, its roles test says alpha exactly 1, and its colourConsts resolver binds same-line const initializers so computed inks like resetInk''s ternary are visible; the donor''s comment re-anchors so propertyValue reaches its color:. Watched red, the sweep names exactly the reset''s ternary and the donor''s entry. Then the reset''s hidden leaf becomes the settings card''s face #101d45 (rgba(99,102,241,0.06) over the sheet, named constant in ColorPicker.tsx) and the donor''s becomes COLORS.surface.sheet. ColorPicker.test.tsx pins the reset''s colour per state (#101d45 default, #5b77a4 shown, #1f3055 custom under a hidden bar); Qibla.test.tsx pins the donor''s ink; the extended resolver is mutation-proven with a planted const ternary. yarn validate green, version bumped."}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3157, 322, 'comment', 'owner', 'Both findings fixed in plan doc v2: the sweep''s colourConsts now binds same-line const initializers and the donor''s comment re-anchors, so the red run names both sites before the swap; and the reset hides against the settings card''s face #101d45 (the card wash flattened over the sheet), not the sheet solid - the donor keeps the sheet solid, where the claim held.', NULL, '2026-10-24 12:46:24.558991+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, 3155, '{}', NULL);
