every reading is transcribed\n- [ ] after the crossing: the day''s remaining prayers still display and fire on time (Fajr observed live), the stored rows for 2026-10-25 serve the day whole on an airplane-mode relaunch with no network, and the reopened app shows the API''s own 25 October values on both schedules\n- [ ] a production build''s alarm dump after the crossing shows every remaining prayer armed at its true local time (Android), and the iOS build''s notifications hold to the same instants\n- [ ] all findings recorded on this ticket as they happen; yarn validate green on any code change"}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3286, 337, 'comment', 'owner', 'Owner order (dictated 2026-10-25, just before the crossing): the watch must also prove NO notification fires incorrectly through the transition - no banner, lock-screen item or sound for a prayer already passed, nothing double-firing through the duplicated 01:00-01:59 wall hour, no re-arm of yesterday''s rows. A correct fire is the Extras 01:00 GMT row at its instant if its bell stands, and Fajr at 05:04 - each exactly once. The post-crossing step inspects the banner history, the lock screen and the armed state; the Fajr step proves the one true fire.', NULL, '2026-10-25 00:16:36.713788+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
