INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3291, 337, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 3 done, the crossing watch transcribed. Four reading sets landed; every time names its zone (BST before the transition, GMT after; the wall fell back 02:00 BST to 01:00 GMT at 01:00:00 UTC).

R1, first 01:xx pass, captured 01:58:51-01:59:03 BST, minutes later than the plan''s 01:55 label (miss reason under R2) but inside the pass. Standard at 01:58:51: clock 01:58, day Sun 25 Oct 2026, countdown Fajr 4h 5m (true remaining 4h05m09s, floor-rendered), rows Fajr 05:04, Sunrise 06:39, Dhuhr 11:50, Asr 14:17, Maghrib 16:50, Isha 18:17, bells silent on Fajr/Sunrise/Isha and speakers on Dhuhr/Asr/Maghrib, all six equal to Step 1''s 25 Oct oracle. Extras at 01:58:56: day Sun 25 Oct 2026, countdown Last Third 1m 5s (true 1m04s, the seconds display rounds up), rows Midnight 23:58, Last Third 01:00 on the highlight, Suhoor 04:44, Duha 06:59. Overlay open on Fajr at 01:59:03: Fajr 4h 4m, list collapsed, day label carried onto the overlay.

R2, the transition. The pre-flip bracket reads at wall 01:59:4x were missed: my wait gate parsed the nonexistent local 02:00:00 as UTC (macOS resolves the duplicated hour''s missing labels as the first occurrence) and anchored an hour late, so the block hung through the flip. The first pass still carries the pre-flip evidence: Standard 4h 4m at 01:59:03 and Extras Last Third 1m 5s at 01:58:56 above. Post-flip, second pass: Standard 01:01:59 GMT, Fajr 4h 2m (true 4h02m01s); Extras 01:02:13 GMT, Suhoor 3h 41m, the target flipped to Suhoor the far side of its instant exactly as the static proof pins, Last Third''s row stays listed with the highlight moved on. No banner frame was caught at the 01:00:00 fire (the same gate miss), so the fire itself has no live evidence tonight; per the plan''s own fallback the fire proof rests on Step 5''s Fajr.

R3, +5 real minutes: Standard 01:05:02 GMT, Fajr 3h 58m (true 3h58m58s); Extras 01:05:08, Suhoor 3h 38m; day Sun 25 Oct 2026 on both; lists identical to the first pass pixel-for-pixel outside clock and countdown. Home-screen read recorded absent, no widget (Step 2''s finding). A bonus pair at 01:02:38/01:02:43 also landed: Standard Fajr 4h 1m, Extras Suhoor 3h 41m.

R4, +15 real minutes: Standard 01:15:03 GMT, Fajr 3h 48m (true 3h48m57s); Extras 01:15:08, Suhoor 3h 28m; overlay on Fajr 01:15:15, Fajr 3h 48m, list collapsed.

Continuity verdict: across six Standard frames from 01:58:51 BST to 01:15:03 GMT the displayed remaining floors the true remaining to the second, every consecutive drop equals the real elapsed seconds, and the total drop across the duplicated hour equals the 16m12s of real time, no stall, no jump, no wall-label echo; the status-bar clock itself fell back between the 01:59 and 01:01 frames. The day label never moved (Sun 25 Oct 2026 on both schedules, both passes, having rolled at Isha''s passing per Step 2): one coherent day through the duplicated hour. Both schedules paged and rendered the whole window, bells unchanged from Step 2.

Lock-screen entries: not taken, and the route analysis is recorded for Steps 4-6. No software lock exists on this runner: Control Centre and Notification Center pulls are rejected inside the top viewport margin, the side button has no emulation, and the runner''s wake tap foregrounds the session''s bound app rather than the lock screen (measured: after a 2-minute Auto-Lock sleep the wake tap landed in Settings, never on the lock screen), while a devicectl launch wakes by relaunching and the launch path runs clearDeliveredNotifications, which would wipe the entries it is meant to read. Auto-Lock was set to 2 minutes for the attempt and is back at Never, verified on the page. No passcode is set (the Settings root carries no Face ID and Passcode row), so any wake bypasses the lock entirely. Note for Step 5: on a sleeping screen a delivered notification may light the lock screen itself, so a screenshot at the fire instant with no wake gesture is the one route left; otherwise the fire evidence is the banner over the foregrounded app.

Device end-state for Step 4: app foregrounded on Standard at 01:45:08 GMT, day Sun 25 Oct 2026, Fajr 3h 18m, rows equal to the oracle, bells as Step 2 left them, Fajr armed for 05:04 GMT.', NULL, '2026-10-25 02:31:10.723145+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3312, 322, 'comment', 'owner', 'Owner''s read (2026-10-25, on the production builds): the reset link perfect, the bold platform words perfect, the single instruction line fixed - every item of the pass and its reopened step verified on glass. The header labels'' ink moved to ticket 344 for its final dim. Closed Done; the lane is merged at 2.4.28.', NULL, '2026-10-25 04:40:54.73851+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
