INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3301, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Owner stand-down order received mid-Step-5; all 3T work from this session stops here. The record for the owner''s own test: the stamp interrogation was Step 4''s (comment 3294) - the version stamp is inert, no What''s New pop, no upgrade work on measured launches. The prod audits had already COMPLETED before the order arrived and their full numbers are in my Step-5 comment below: the production 2.4.24 build (real API, no mock churn possible) still showed the tap-adjacent dead zones (333-851ms, inside the cross-build band), the settings sheet rendered clean from 24 percent both passes, the alert sheet rendered clean once and snapped at 96 percent on the second run, and the close fade read four-to-five alpha steps against the baseline era''s nine - the failure signature is version- and env-invariant, not the mock env''s churn, and predates 2.4.11 or the capture layer degraded since September. Device state as I left it: the owner''s prod line on the 3T was upgraded 2.4.22 to 2.4.24 (same signer, data kept) for the experiment, armed per its stored prefs, HOME, no agents - the lead''s 2.4.28 install supersedes it. No further installs, audits or driving from this session. Subtask 332 stays as the lead set it; the owner''s own production testing takes it from here.', NULL, '2026-10-25 03:51:23.731554+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3302, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Owner order (2026-10-25): the owner takes the performance verdict personally on the production builds - subtask 332 closes owner-tested. The stood-down experiment''s partial record stands: the dead zones persist on the production build (333-851ms, inside the cross-build band), so the signature is invariant across version and environment; the surviving candidates are a regression predating the 2.4.11 window or a degraded capture layer since the September baselines. The owner''s read on 2.4.28 prod decides which; the lane re-plans only if the owner still feels the jank.', NULL, '2026-10-25 03:52:30.027332+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3303, 337, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 4 stood down mid-proof by owner order: the XS passed into the owner''s hand. This is the partial record, per the stand-down. Subtask 341 left unticked for the lead.

The offline stored-rows proof, Extras schedule - landed whole. With airplane mode on and Wi-Fi off (airplane icon in the status bar, wifi fan and signal dots gone), the app was relaunched at 02:44 GMT and served the day from stored rows alone: day label Sun 25 Oct 2026, rows Midnight 23:58, Last Third 01:00, Suhoor 04:44, Duha 06:59, every row equal to Step 1''s oracle and pixel-identical to the online read taken at 02:36-02:37; countdown alive on Suhoor 1h 59m (true remaining 1h59m41s, correct rounding); no error banner, no spinner, no offline notice anywhere on screen. Nothing re-fetched wrongly: the radio-off relaunch rendered the same day the online app had. The online reopen after the airplane cycle (02:45) showed the same oracle rows again.

Owner orders carried: the Suhoor 04:44 and Duha 06:59 reminders display at exactly those times in every Extras frame, online and offline, Suhoor carrying the live highlight (their fires remain Step 5''s). The no-wrong-fire inspection: no banner, alert or overlay sits over the app in any frame from 02:36 to 03:26; banner history and Notification Center stay unreadable on this passcode-less phone (the atlas''s measured rejection), so the 01:15-02:36 gap has no witness - named, not invented. The Extras bells read unchanged from Step 2 (four bell glyphs, none slashed).

One anomaly, recorded without adjudication. At 03:23-03:26 the Standard page served values matching neither the 25 nor the 26 Oct oracle: Fajr 03:24 with Sunrise 03:34 (a ten-minute gap London never has), Dhuhr 13:04, Asr 16:56, Maghrib 20:14, Isha 21:27, and the Fajr row''s own time advancing minute-by-minute with the clock across three frames, under a Hijri date label (Jumada I 14, 1448) where every earlier frame read Sun 25 Oct 2026. That pattern matches launch-relative rather than API data. I ran no device action between 02:45 and 03:23 (transcription only); the owner''s 01:47 order says the owner was enabling reminders on this phone tonight. The Standard page''s post-crossing reads therefore do not stand as oracle evidence; the Standard offline frame (03:25) rendered a whole six-row day under airplane but its values carry the same anomaly. Also named: Step 3''s handover note said Standard foregrounded, while my at-rest frame at 02:36 found the Extras page.

Missing readings: the Standard schedule''s post-crossing display against the oracle (anomalous, above), and the 3T post-crossing alarm dump (the extension never ran; the 3T was Lane 2''s tonight). The reopened-shows-API-values clause is proven for Extras alone.

Airplane mode was toggled twice for the proof (02:39-02:45, 03:24-03:26) and restored off both times. Device state as I left it at 03:26:21 GMT: unlocked, airplane off, Wi-Fi back on the home network, cellular normal, app foregrounded on the Standard page, battery full. Nothing touched since. The eight transcribed frames remain in this session''s temp directory for Step 6 if needed.', NULL, '2026-10-25 03:55:40.516232+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
