INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3299, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 5 done: the decisive experiment ran, and it takes branch two - the production build still dead-zones, so the frame failures are not the mock env''s churn. The regression is real against the September baselines, predates 2.4.11 (or the capture layer degraded since September; tonight cannot separate those two), and widening the bisect is a re-planned step, not improvised here.

The build and the install. uat 2.4.24 (1c22014c) built as PRODUCTION through build-prod.zsh: EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod, the real API key in the bundle, package <pkg>, versionCode 1000000, versionName 2.4.24, the owner''s debug certificate, built locally in 489s. FOR THE RECORD: this install REPLACED THE OWNER''S PROD LINE ON THE 3T, 2.4.22 to 2.4.24, same signer, adb install -r, data kept, User 0 alone - the daily line now carries 2.4.24. Controls: battery 67 to 71 percent on USB charge, saver off, no screensharing agent, the dev package (com.example.athan, 2.4.23) force-stopped before every audit, first post-install launch discarded, force-stops between flows, the 1-second pre-tap close variant, tap points re-verified from the live tree (row and bell at y~1012, settings 539,1833 - identical to Steps 3 and 4; the tree reads the real timetable Fajr 05:04 to Isha 18:17, so boundaries sat 95 minutes to 15 hours out and nothing could shift mid-audit). No committed flow was driven; no repository change was made.

The numbers, prod beside the mock band. Tap-to-first-drawn-change dead zones: 333-851ms across all four interactions and both passes - inside the mock band Steps 1, 3 and 4 recorded (176-927ms across 2.4.11-2.4.24), on the shipping env. Entrances: the settings sheet RENDERED clean both passes (first drawn frame 23.9 and 23.8 percent of travel, a dozen decelerating positions, ten graduated scrim steps); the alert sheet rendered pass 1 (43.4 percent first frame, ten decelerating positions, graduated scrim) and SNAPPED pass 2 (first drawn frame 96.4 percent traveled, four moving frames, scrim 0 to full in one step) - the exact signature Step 1 read as the tip''s regression, produced by the prod build on a second run, with the vision reads explicitly confirming ZERO churn signatures in all eight recordings: no row shifts, no selection-pill slides, no overlay auto-close or re-open, no data hard-cuts, no countdown ticks. Overlay-open: the first post-tap change is the countdown header swap at 10 percent of travel inside the dead zone, then veil ramps of four to five opacity steps with the first motion frame at 12 to 34 percent veil, plus one genuine 66ms mid-entrance freeze (three duplicate rendered frames) in pass 1. Overlay-close: the overlay was genuinely open at recording start both passes (on prod the 2-second close window cannot fire with boundaries hours away, so the mock''s auto-close failure mode is structurally absent), graduated fades of five and four distinct alpha levels after a 300-400ms dead zone; the baseline era''s nine-alpha close reads four to five tonight - on prod exactly as on every mock build this week, the capture-loss fingerprint, env-invariant.

The verdict. The mock-churn hypothesis for the FRAME failures is refuted by experiment: churn is absent and the failures persist. The signature - a tap-adjacent dead zone plus entrance first-draws that land anywhere from 24 to 96 percent run-to-run - is version-invariant (2.4.11 through 2.4.24) and env-invariant (mock and prod). Against the 2026-09-11/12 baselines, which measured these same interactions at the floor on this same phone, the regression is real and predates 2.4.11, or the SD820''s capture path reads worse than it did six weeks ago; tonight''s instrument cannot separate compositor truth from encoder loss inside the dead zone, and the plan''s Step 6 (post-fix proof) cannot run as written because there is no fix to prove. What the experiment does settle for the owner: the mock line''s day-to-day behavior (per-launch reseed, boundary-adjacent auto-close, rows shifting under the overlay, the per-launch refresh) is real mock-only behavior and part of what the owner feels on the recently-mock phone - none of it appears on the prod line - but the floor failures stand on the shipping line too, so the felt regression is not only the mock build.

What the re-planned step must do: separate the compositor from the encoder (a same-tap SurfaceFlinger latency capture beside the video recording - a harness change with its own commit - or an equivalent present-timestamp read inside a recorded run); rebuild a pre-2.4.11 baseline-era anchor and measure it tonight to date the dead zone''s entry against the September floor passes; and hold the baselines honest until then - mock-window discipline stays binding for any mock-env audit (evening seeds minutes from boundaries, the stock 3s pre-tap close unusable on mock), floor verdicts only from prod-env or boundary-far runs. The committed flows'' APP_ID breakage and stale tap points remain open harness debt as Step 4 recorded. Evidence dirs, worktree-local and untracked: prod-p1-overlay-open-032014, prod-p1-overlay-close-032035, prod-p1-sheet-alert-open-032057, prod-p1-sheet-settings-open-032119, prod-p2-overlay-open-032155, prod-p2-overlay-close-032216, prod-p2-sheet-alert-open-032238, prod-p2-sheet-settings-open-032300. The lane branch stands at 2.4.25 (4ffd1f34); no commit was needed - no harness file was touched, the 1s variant lived in session temp.', NULL, '2026-10-25 03:38:25.648143+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', '2026-10-25 05:37:10.057+00');
