- Verified: the new item sits inside the content contract and the translation lock. Mutants, each killed by name: an en body over 96 chars fails "WHATS_NEW content contract - item ''What''s New'' has a non-empty body within the limit"; an ms body reverted to its en source fails "ms carries no archive copy equal to its en source"; the debut stamp moved to 2.5.0 fails both "archives the What''s New screen itself, stamped at its 1.13.0 debut" and "stays silent for a reader who has seen the newest feature, debut included".
- Verified: df08bfb1 (2026-08-30, "1.13.0 - feat(whats-new)") is the first commit that touched shared/whatsNew.ts and it created the modal, so the 1.13.0 stamp is the true debut.
