INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3497, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 10 record (the dual-instrument verdict on the tip, T-355): measured on the 3T against Step 2''s both-platform tip build, REUSED not rebuilt - the APK from the step-2 session (uat tip dc269768, com.example.athan, Release gate-ON, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1, mock env, arm64-v8a), badging re-asserted before install (package com.example.athan, versionName 2.4.40), adb install -r, User 0 alone, first launch discarded, marks verified flowing. D12''s both-platforms rule was satisfied by the step-2 session; the build slot stayed free tonight. Battery 100 percent on USB charge for every run; no screensharing agents (top checked); the second Athan-family package force-stopped before every capture and flow; D11 held throughout (each frame-audit capture relaunches and reseeds, and its recording window ends ~17s after launch while the seeded boundary lands ~60-90s out; the marks flows ran Step 2''s ritual - fresh launch, 185s roll so the boundary sits hours out, then drive).

THE INSTRUMENT ON GLASS (Step 9''s validation): the dual read as committed is honest in its video half and broken in its SF half on this phone. Two defects. (1) The clock anchor: tap_uptime.txt reads /proc/uptime (CLOCK_BOOTTIME, suspend included) while SF presents ride CLOCK_MONOTONIC (suspend excluded); this phone carries ~8047s of accumulated suspend, so the committed window filter rejects every real present and admits only the sentinel row - every capture printed a garbage first draw (~9.2e12 ms) and "SF 30fps FLOOR: NO DATA" with exit 1. (2) The sentinel row: dumpsys''s trailing row carries INT64_MAX in column 2, which the !=0 filter keeps. The committed script ran unmodified for all eight captures (its outputs are in the evidence dirs); the verdicts below come from a session post-processor fixing exactly those two things (per-capture suspend offset anchored by clear-ring + tap + uptime-read-in-one-shell; col3 = actual present; the pairing logic is the committed script''s own, unchanged). The pair script and drivers sit in e2e/evidence/step10-driver/ for the lane to lift into frame-audit.sh before Step 11 - until then the script''s PRINTED SF verdicts are void on any phone that has ever suspended, which is every phone. Anchor discipline learned on glass: the anchor tap is itself a transition, and taps that close a sheet present 275-296ms late, so such anchors read LOW; offsets cannot decrease (suspend only adds), so the true offset is the highest coherent reading - two polluted anchors were substituted (notes in their dirs), and the phone dozed ~430ms once between captures (screen timeout in a gap).

THE VERDICTS, n=2 per interaction (per capture: video dead zones vs SF dead zones; first draw video vs SF, +-50-70ms anchor):

- overlay-open: ENCODER LOSS on the tap-adjacent dead zone, both runs. Run 091238: video 50ms@+415, 1053ms@+733, 253ms@+1804 vs SF 52ms@-36, 1063ms@+265, 822ms@+1331, 60ms@+2153; first draw 415ms vs -36ms. Run 092047: video 50ms@+294, 1057ms@+611 vs SF 48ms@-6, 1068ms@+295; first draw 294ms vs -6ms. The compositor presents within a vsync of the tap and runs the entrance at 16-28ms; the encoder misses the entrance''s first ~300-400ms. The entrance''s own opening hiccup (one 48-52ms gap) is compositor-real in both runs; the post-entrance idle gaps pair trivially (both idle).
- overlay-close: ENCODER LOSS on the tap-adjacent dead zone, both runs; the close entrance itself carries REAL compositor gaps. Run 092200: video 52@+244, 34@+377, 36@+527, 591@+579, 1001@+1186 vs SF 61@-33, 46@+243, 589@+307, 1006@+901; first draw 244 vs -33ms. Run 092327: video 34@+476, 74@+577, 352@+664, 989@+1032 vs SF 71@+234, 364@+320, 993@+688; first draw 281 vs -17ms. SF cadence inside the close shows one to two gaps of 46-71ms - the close genuinely stutters at compositor level while the open does not.
- sheet-alert-open: MIXED - the tap-adjacent delay is compositor-shared, the entrance-early frames are encoder-lost. Run 092359: video 134@+313, 50@+447, 169@+2042 vs SF 134@+58, 47@+192, 170@+1776; first draw 62 vs 58ms - BOTH instruments wait ~60ms, then the compositor stalls 134ms before running a clean 17ms entrance (all three zones corroborated). Run 092542: video 285@+299, 273@+1905 vs SF 275@+1512, 457@+1801, 160@+2269; first draw 116 vs 184ms; SF cadence PASS (84 gaps all <=27ms) - once the sheet starts presenting it holds 60fps; the encoder still loses the entrance''s early frames.
- sheet-settings-open: COMPOSITOR TRUTH on the tap-adjacent dead zone. Run 092644: video 84@+7, 50@+125, 100@+292, 447@+1117, 90@+1582, 360@+1692 vs SF 89@+126, 45@+246, 109@+407, 460@+1236, 466@+1705; SF''s first ~500ms is ragged at compositor level (gaps 45, 78, 89, 109ms) before settling to 17ms. Run 092755: video 233@+134, 140@+1020, 132@+1995 vs SF 34@+225, 228@+313, 140@+1196, 128@+2173; first draw 36 vs 208ms - the 228ms tap-adjacent zone corroborated in size and position.
- Independent corroboration from the anchor taps themselves: the two anchor taps that closed a sheet presented 275-296ms late, while every overlay-driving anchor tap presented immediately - the sheet paths'' tap-to-present delay is compositor-real, the overlay paths'' is not.
- Universal across all eight captures: a late ~100-250ms present burst on BOTH instruments ~1.7-2.2s after the tap (idle zones 822-1068ms, then a short run). Real compositor activity, source unidentified - the vision read should name it (candidates: H2''s hold-then-hide timers, the ago badge, the info-box fade).

Net answer to the step''s question: the campaign''s tap-adjacent dead zone is two different things. On the overlay open/close it is ENCODER LOSS (the compositor presents at the tap; the video''s 244-415ms of nothing is the encoder dropping the entrance''s early frames). On the sheets it is substantially COMPOSITOR TRUTH (a real ~60-208ms tap-to-present delay, plus a ragged 45-109ms first half-second on settings), with encoder loss layered on top. Step 11 should read the overlay paths as encoder-dominated and the sheet paths as compositor-bearing.

MARKS, through the now-honest committed flows (n=10 each; baseline column from e2e/baselines/android-3t.json, whose overlay rows are the stale pre-s9 240s per its own 2026-09-11 note):
- overlay_open 145 (baseline 240, delta -95; standing band 134-156) - no regression
- overlay_close 148 (240, -92; band 139-158) - no regression
- sheet_alert_open 454 (456, -2; band 429-456) - no regression
- sheet_settings_open 384 (370, +14; band 368-392) - no regression
- sheet_settings_close 210 (202, +8; band 204-210) - no regression
- sheet_alert_close 206 (no baseline row; band 204-210) - no regression
- sheet_alert_open_anim 194 / sheet_settings_open_anim 196 - no baseline rows (newer sub-mark)
Marks never regressed, again; every median sits inside the standing cross-build bands.

Close-point verification: the committed overlay-close point 540,1100 still closes the overlay - verified from the live tree and behaviorally. The overlay''s veil tiles "Close prayer details" around the highlighted row (bottom tile [0,1057][1080,1920]); the 38px list lift moved the Asr row node over the point but the veil still owns the tap (after tapping it the tree carries zero Close nodes and the home asserts). NO follow-up fix needed to the flow. Bell 979,1012 (inside [910,907][1049,1057]) and settings 539,1833 (exact button center) verified from the live tree before driving.

Vision reads: NOT done this session - it is a nested subagent (depth limit) and cannot spawn the vision subagent, and the model takes no image input. Per the step''s fallback the printed paired gap lists stand as the evidence; all eight vision-prompt.md files sit ready in their evidence dirs for the lane to arrange the read.

Device state as left: the 3T on the measured 2.4.40 dev build at User 0 alone, app foregrounded on the home screen, battery 100 percent on USB charge; the owner line untouched except force-stops; no worktree changes (evidence dirs untracked).

Evidence dirs (worktree-local, untracked): e2e/evidence/overlay-open-091238, overlay-open-092047, overlay-close-092200, overlay-close-092327, sheet-alert-open-092359, sheet-alert-open-092542, sheet-settings-open-092644, sheet-settings-open-092755, marks-overlay-092913, marks-sheets-093412, step10-driver/ (pair script, drivers, anchor notes).

For Step 11''s driver: fold the two instrument fixes (monotonic anchor + sentinel filter) into frame-audit.sh first, or run the committed script and post-process with e2e/evidence/step10-driver/t327-pair.py; per-capture anchors are mandatory (dozes happen between captures; sheet-closing anchor taps pollute LOW - take the highest coherent offset). At 1.25.0: adb install -d for the era''s lower versionCode, its own yarn.lock governs, its e2e/README.md is the ritual of record, and the baseline''s own _sf_latency_note already warns SF single runs are not reproducible - the interleaved A/B/A answers that. Read the overlay paths against the encoder-loss finding and the sheet paths against the compositor-truth finding; if the anchor shows the same split, the September-vs-today difference is instrument-era, and if the anchor''s sheets present at the tap, a code regression in the sheet paths entered 1.25.0..2.4.11.', NULL, '2026-10-25 09:41:53.045068+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3498, 355, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'status', '2026-10-25 10:34:40.725289+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"id": 4, "value": "Done", "stateType": "completed"}, "from": {"id": 1, "value": "Backlog", "stateType": "backlog"}}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3499, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 10''s vision read is in and completes the evidence; it agrees with the SF separation. The settings sheet''s dead zone is compositor truth (a real 33.6ms freeze at 93 percent of travel then a 110px jump in one run, an 87.4 percent snap in the other), the alert sheet''s onset stall is real (roughly the first quarter of its travel never presented), and the overlay''s tap-adjacent holes are encoder loss - though the close entrance carries real compositor gaps of 46-71ms. The instrument''s SF clock anchor takes the fix Step 10''s record names before Step 11 relies on it.', NULL, '2026-10-25 10:34:40.769974+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3500, 346, 'comment', 'owner', 'Agent-ruled (step 3): the S23 is not attached and no other Android phone is, so the OnePlus 3T takes the Android read - both panels are ~360dp wide, so the same Hindi badge wraps or holds identically. Plan doc''s device line amended.', NULL, '2026-10-25 10:43:00.72412+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3501, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 11''s instrument fold is landed: lane1/T-327 at ed6a06a2 (2.4.42, validate green 232 suites) - the dual run now measures the suspend offset itself per capture (ring clear, anchor tap, uptime read in one shell, dump) and pairs on CLOCK_MONOTONIC, the INT64_MAX sentinel row drops, and the read moves to the third latency column (the actual present); SF_OFFSET overrides a polluted LOW anchor, and the README Gotcha carries the anchor discipline. All verdict paths desk-verified against synthetic captures. Step 11 (the 1.25.0-era anchor, A/B/A against the kept tip APK) waits on Lane 2''s build slot and phones (T-346''s T-367).', NULL, '2026-10-25 10:52:55.757286+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3502, 346, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 3''s device reads are in, on the 2.4.46 mock build of this branch. The 3T (standing in for the unattached S23, agent-ruled above) read all six locales: every badge renders on one line, Hindi''s sentence whole with no cropped second line, Thai''s gap around the time measuring the same as the sentence''s own word spacing, and English, Arabic, Malay and Somali undisturbed. The XS read Thai and Hindi: Thai carries the space before and after the time, and Hindi holds one line. The strings were read from live view dumps and the pixels from measured screenshots kept out of the repository.', NULL, '2026-10-25 11:48:15.098346+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
