INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3574, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 11 record (the baseline-era anchor dated, T-356): the anchor 6478619b (1.25.0) built fresh this session from its own yarn.lock (badging asserted com.example.athan 1.25.0; adb install -d is refused for a release APK on Android 9, so each anchor install was uninstall plus install, first launch discarded, marks verified flowing; the era''s iOS canary compiled green on today''s toolchain and was recorded, never installed), and the A/B/A ran interleaved on one night against the kept tip APK (2.4.40, badging re-asserted): anchor, tip, anchor, plus a corrective anchor pair - 26 driven dual captures and 7 recorder-free controls, battery 100/full throughout, the second Athan-family package force-stopped before every capture, the 3T left on the 2.4.40 tip at User 0 alone as found.

THE VERDICT: the degradation branch. The September floors do not reproduce on this phone tonight on EITHER build. The anchor - the baselines'' own commit - fails the SF cadence on all 16 of its valid captures (entrance gaps 100-317ms) with the recorder running, and still bumps 34-96ms recorder-free; the tip holds 16-17ms recorder-free but its sheets stall 304-468ms under the recorder tonight, where the same APK read 45-109ms ragged this morning (Step 10). The recorder is now a participant, not a witness: the era app idles near 25 percent CPU by its own baseline note, and recorder load turns that headroom deficit into compositor stalls; the tip''s sheets have drifted the same direction within one day. The 1.25.0..2.4.11 code window is REFUTED - the September-smooth build is the jankier one tonight. Step 12 records the degradation dossier and the question goes to the owner.

The vision read (every frame seen, 26 sheets): the anchor''s entrances are monotone with no snap wherever the encoder sampled them (overlay 8-18 intermediate frames; sheets rigid-body translations), the tip''s overlay close keeps its two-stage hold-then-snap tail, and every entrance''s earliest travel is under-sampled on video on both builds - the campaign''s video dead zones are holes in the record, not visible freezes. Discarded per discipline: four anchor settings captures drove a wrong point (a hierarchy bounds scan took the page-dots strip for the gear glyph; the true center is 540,1768, and the corrective pair re-ran there, both settling clean - the behavioral verify catches what a bounds scan misses) and one tip overlay-open caught the mock rollover (the seeded minute boundary landed inside its record).

Instrument notes for Step 12: per-capture SF anchors read 8047.0-8047.64 all night, highest coherent 8047.642, used as SF_OFFSET where the hardcoded anchor tap at y1012 lands inside the taller evening-state settings sheet; the tip''s list sits at y982 in the evening state versus y1012 in the morning - the row''s y rides the mock state and both readings stay inside the same 150px row. Evidence: e2e/evidence/step11-driver/ (the driver, the entrance reader, SUMMARY, per-capture logs) plus the 30 capture dirs, all untracked in the lane worktree; the anchor APK kept beside the step-2 tip at ~/athan-gitree/sessions/t327-step11/artifacts/. Lane hygiene: the resident athan-smoke-28 AVD was killed at session start per the README rule (disk state kept; it sat abandoned on a GMS dialog).', NULL, '2026-10-25 17:13:14.969271+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
