INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3576, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 12 record (the degradation dossier, T-357): Step 11 handed the degradation branch, so per the plan''s tree this step records the dossier and the question goes to the owner - no bisect runs, no fix, Steps 13-15 collapse per the plan''s own ruling.

The dossier''s measurements, tonight, daytime, battery 100/full on USB throughout, owner-line package force-stopped, no screensharing agents: idle CPU past the 5.5-minute mock window reads the anchor at 22.2 percent (lower bound) against its own September note''s 24.8 - the era app''s draw is STABLE - and the tip at 16.0, better than both. Thermal and battery rule themselves out: 29.3-30.1C all session, every thermal zone 29-37C, no throttle band approached. So the degradation is not app CPU cost, not charge, not heat: the phone and its recorder now convert the same app load into compositor stalls that September recorded as 16-17ms cadence, and the same tip APK moved its sheets from 45-109ms (morning) to 304-468ms (tonight) under the recorder with unchanged bytes. The XS control is instrument-independent (syslog marks plus the owner''s eyeball; no encoder, no SF, no screenrecord), so its smooth verdict and its Step 2 bands stand untouched by this finding - and tonight they agree with the 3T''s recorder-free 16-17ms tip cadence; what contradicts both is the recorder-on record and the owner''s own recorder-free hand on 2.4.28 production. That tension is the question.

Evidence: e2e/evidence/step12-dossier/ in the lane worktree (SUMMARY, both idle runs with raw per-thread samples, battery and thermal snapshots), untracked; the worktree and its branch stand for the ruling. The 3T is left on the 2.4.40 tip at User 0 alone as found; the anchor and tip APKs stay preserved under ~/athan-gitree/sessions/. No commit this step - the degradation branch demands no tracked-file change, and the version-bump rule rides commits that do not exist.', NULL, '2026-10-25 17:37:25.001795+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
