2. Step 2: the ruled outcome measured on the simulators (device, 3 points). Runs alone in a fresh executor session. Read e2e/README.md''s Gotchas first. Version bump first (patch), then build from the branch: npx expo run:ios -d SIMULATOR_UDID --configuration Release. On the iPhone Duo simulator (iOS 27.1): open pose, landscape - the window spans 951x669, the gradient reads edge to edge with no pure-black side bars, the countdown and schedule centred in the 500pt column; open pose, portrait hold - the 669x951 window class, layout centred, the delivered top and bottom insets transcribed; half-open pose - the same spanning window class as open, no scaled window, no phantom inset; the clamp verdict recorded across all three open-pose readings (identity, or the Decision 5 park); closed pose - a rotation attempt refused, the window in today''s 466x678 class, rendering equal to today; an open-closed-open round trip - the process stays live and each pose renders its own geometry. On the phone-class simulator (iPhone 18 Pro class, iOS 27.0): rotation attempts in both directions refuse; the snapshot stays portrait. One spanning-landscape screenshot attached to this row from scratch outside the worktree, never committed; SIMULATOR_UDID placeholder in every committed record. Snapshot, one commit.
3. Step 2b: the live-unfold re-span lands or is recorded impossible (code, 2 points). Step 2''s measurement found that a process launched folded keeps the 469x669 letterbox on live unfold until relaunch: UIKit does not re-ask the supported orientations when the window changes panels, so the spanning only arrives at the next launch. The ruling''s own words cover this path ("to remove the black letterbox bars"), and this step is Risk 1''s fix branch executed on the open side. Extend plugins/duoLandscapeGate.js with an exported pure editSceneDelegate that inserts into SceneDelegate an override of the iOS-13 UIWindowSceneDelegate callback windowScene(_:didUpdate:interfaceOrientation:traitCollection:) - the callback UIKit fires when the scene''s coordinate space changes, which a panel change is - whose body calls window?.rootViewController?.setNeedsUpdateOfSupportedInterfaceOrientations() (Apple: "Notifies the view controller about a change in supported interface orientations"). Tests red-first, mirroring the AppDelegate suite (insertion once, idempotence, marker throw, the literal selector pin). Version bump, prebuild, rebuild, then measure only the unfold-live path: launch closed, unfold, read the window class and the panel-edge pixels; re-verify the closed refusal and the fresh-open spanning beside it. If the letterbox persists, the same callback body gains the bounded fallback - requestGeometryUpdate(.iOS(interfaceOrientations:)) with the four, called only when the window scene''s screen is the Duo inner display class - and the unfold-live path is measured once more. If both attempts fail, the SceneDelegate insertion is reverted (the AppDelegate gate stays), and the limitation is recorded on the row with the attempt''s evidence. Comment, snapshot, one commit.
4. Step 3: the row''s records closed (docs, 1 point). Read the branch diff and record that it names exactly the plugin, its test, app.json, the version files and board/snapshot/board.sql, plus the inset files when the owner-ordered exemption ran, so no phone-tuned layout value moved; tick the subtasks; regenerate the snapshot. Version bump, snapshot, one commit.

- Live unfold re-spans without a relaunch, or the limitation is recorded: Step 2b''s transcribed unfold-live reading on this row.

## Risks

- UIKit may not re-ask the mask when the fold closes: the closed pose would keep landscape until the next ask. Shows as the closed pose accepting rotation after the round trip in Step 2. Fix branch: the SceneDelegate observes the scene''s screen change and calls setNeedsUpdateOfSupportedInterfaceOrientations on the root view controller.
- The delegate may be asked with a nil window early in launch: the gate fails closed (portrait pair); the worst case on the open Duo is a portrait presentation until the next ask. Shows as a letterboxed or portrait launch frame in Step 2. Fix branch: key on the first connected UIWindowScene''s screen when the window is nil.
- An open-pose top inset above 62: the row parks in Awaiting Owner per Decision 5 instead of landing a clamp change; the spanning background still ships, only the inset honoring waits on the owner.
- A future SDK may change the AppDelegate template: the marker edit throws at prebuild, never silently no-ops, and the unit tests pin the marker against the current template shape.
- Resizable-window contexts (iPhone Mirroring, iPad resizing) treat orientations as a preference on iOS 27+ (Expo SDK 58 docs): outside the verified fence, which covers full-screen phones, the Duo''s poses and full-screen iPads. Recorded, not chased.
- The panel class constant is exact points: a future Duo hardware revision with a different inner panel fails closed to portrait. Recorded, not chased; the constant is named for exactly this read.

## Proof

- Gate named and implemented: Step 1''s prebuild read (the gate in AppDelegate.swift, the four in the iPhone array, ~ipad still portrait-only) and the test suite pinning masks, constants, idempotence and wiring.
- Duo open landscape spans, no bars, centred, transcribed: Step 2''s transcribed readings on this row, plus the attached screenshot.
- Closed pose stays portrait: Step 2''s transcribed refusal and window class on this row.
- No physical iPhone rotates, gate unit-tested: Step 2''s transcribed rotation refusals on the phone-class simulator; the plugin test suite.
- Otherwise unchanged, validate green: Step 3''s recorded branch diff naming no layout value; the phone simulator''s portrait snapshot equal to today''s; yarn validate green at every step commit.


## Audit (2026-10-20)

Both reviews on uat..lane/271 came back sound (comments 2593 plan-conformance, 2597 blind); each re-ran the suites green in the worktree. Then the owner''s final ruling (comment 2585, 05:17) landed between execution''s close and the reviews'' dispatch: Option A is cancelled completely, the landscape-span gate never merges, uat carries none of it, and the Duo''s answer is Option B on row 280 (portrait-tall, rendered top-down, background edge to edge). Row 280''s plan already records the disposition ("Option A documented in one line: cancelled by the owner''s final ruling, never merged").

Findings adjudicated, all moot on a dead branch and recorded for Option B''s builder: the dead ALL_ORIENTATIONS export and the unmet README rule (no user-facing feature ships); the duplicate JS/Swift comment; the sentinel''s fail-open on template drift (key any future sentinel on the gate''s own helper signature, not the override selector); the super bypass of Expo''s subscriber manager. The conformance reviewer''s commit list corrected: the branch carried four commits - 767bb1d9 2.1.34 (the gate), aceab2fc 2.1.35 (the measurements), 825e832f 2.1.36 (Step 2b closed with the limitation), b8d1a358 2.1.37 (the records) - all deleted with the branch by the ruling, none merged.

