INSERT INTO public.project_document (id, project_id, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, archived_by_ancestor_id, "position", version, owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, updated_by_user_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (34, 1, NULL, 'T-322', '# T-322 — A visual polish pass: the colour modal''s backdrop, the 3T''s reset ink, the header labels'' ink, the qibla sheet''s doubled instruction text, and bold platform words in Help

## Goal

Five visual defects stand on uat today: the colour modal opens with no dimming behind it, the reset control renders a black word on the 3T instead of hiding, the two header labels carry one ink in both home and overlay states, the qibla sheet''s header shows a doubled darker line while the calibration runs, and Help''s widget answer carries its platform words in the same weight as the sentence. When this ticket is done, the modal dims exactly as the other bottom sheets do, the reset hides in ink that no platform renders black, each header label carries its tuned home ink and its tuned overlay ink, the qibla header shows exactly one instruction line, and the platform words read bold in all six shipped locales. The owner reads every item on glass; the lane ships code, tests and a green `yarn validate`, nothing else.

Planned against uat f97cd7d4 (2.4.17), which carries ticket 294''s colour-carried dim whole. The ticket''s planning note named 294''s conversion as the prime suspect for the reset ink and the doubled qibla line: verified. Both defects are `color: ''transparent''` on a Text — alpha-0 ink, which Android paints black. They are the only two alpha-0 text colours left in app/ and components/ (the settings sheet''s grabber and other named colours are opaque).

**Reopened 2026-10-24** (owner''s read on the 2.4.22 production mock build, both phones): the qibla criterion alone is unmet — the compass sheet still shows doubled instruction text, the bright ''Follow below instructions'' line with dark text stacked over it, on the iPhone as well as Android. Everything else in the pass stood approved, merged at 2.4.23. The reopened pass adds Step 5 below; Steps 1-4 shipped and their sections stand as history.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 — The two Android black-ink defects are one defect class: alpha-0 text ink. Each site stops hiding in alpha-0 ink and paints the literal face it sits on: the qibla donor paints `COLORS.surface.sheet` (#0b183a, the face its own crossfade sibling already interpolates to), and the reset paints the settings card''s face `#101d45` — the card wash `rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.06)` flattened over the sheet, rgb(16,29,69), carried as a named constant in ColorPicker.tsx beside the file''s existing flatten constants. Why two faces: the reset row sits inside the Countdown Bar card (Settings.tsx `styles.card`), so sheet-solid glyphs would print a dark word on both platforms; the donor sits on the bare sheet header, where the sheet solid is exact.
- 2026-10-24 — The text-ink sweep inside `yarn validate` is tightened to ban alpha-0 outright AND its `colourConsts` resolver is extended to bind any same-line `const` initializer, so a computed ink like `resetInk`''s ternary is visible to the check; the donor''s `color:` declaration is re-anchored (its comment moves) so `propertyValue` reaches it. Why: the griller proved the tightened sweep alone names neither site — the ternary const resolves no leaf and the comment blocks the property anchor — so the ban would be vacuous. The red run is observable: with both changes in and both sites still carrying `''transparent''`, the sweep names exactly those two.
- 2026-10-24 — The colour modal''s backdrop is `COLORS.surface.backdrop` (#000116) composited at the 0.9 the shared `renderBackdrop` passes, pre-composited as one rgba constant because the overlay View must not dim its own children. A pinning test derives the constant from `COLORS.surface.backdrop`, so the modal and the sheets cannot drift apart. Tap-outside dismissal is unchanged: the acceptance asks for the dimming alone.
- 2026-10-24 — The header labels'' tuned inks are two new `COLORS.text` roles derived from today''s shared ink #6c79c2 (h231 s41 l59) by measured shifts: home `#7485b9` (hue to 225, toward the band behind''s #031a4c at h221; saturation to 33, the blue-grey; lightness held) and overlay `#7173bc` (hue to 238, toward the glow''s #5b1eaa at h266; saturation to 36, the greyer; lightness held). Why: the owner gave direction, not values; these are one small step from today''s ink in the named directions, and the owner''s glass read is the bar. Countdown''s label rides the `overlayProgress` it already computes; Day''s location rides the `showOverlayDate` flag its masjid already rides — no new atoms.
- 2026-10-24 — Help''s bold platform words split at render time on the pinned Latin labels (`iOS: ` / `Android: `), bolding the label run in the app''s emphasis face. The six catalogs are untouched. Why: the shipped widget copy is byte-pinned with Latin labels in every locale (owner-ruled D142.11) and hash-locked; splitting at render keeps that contract and needs no lock churn.
- 2026-10-24 — Versioning: every commit runs `git fetch origin` first and takes the next free patch number above the highest it sees (uat is 2.4.17, so 2.4.18 or higher), bumping `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` and `shared/whatsNew.ts` together. Patch class throughout: no step types its subject `feat`. No prebuild, no build, no install — the owner ordered code only.
- 2026-10-24 (reopened) — Root cause ruled from the code on uat 887d7949: the subtitle''s colour crossfade paints BOTH of its lines permanently, and while the calibration runs the ready line — absolutely positioned and declared after the waiting line, so it paints over it — rests its ink at `COLORS.surface.sheet` #0b183a. That ink is invisible against the sheet face but sits directly over the waiting line''s bright #416899 glyphs, so where the two sentences'' glyphs cross, dark navy covers bright blue: glyph-shaped dark text over the bright line, both platforms, by construction (two opaque paints at one position, later declaration on top; nothing platform-specific remains). At the settled end the stack is the other way round — the bright ready line on top, the waiting line''s #0b183a beneath — where an under-paint that equals the face is invisible under every part of the upper glyphs, anti-aliased edges included, which is why the settled sheet reads clean and the calibrating sheet does not. The owner''s quoted copy settles which arm is which: ''Follow below instructions'' is `qibla.subtitleWaiting` (en.ts:133), the bright line shown while the calibration runs. The 150 ms fade between the two states stacks interpolated inks the same way, so the transition itself also reads doubled. Step 2''s donor fix was correct (the Android black ghost below the pair) but was the smaller half. The wave line is exonerated: `QiblaCalibration`''s headline and message paint #fff and #416899, mount only while calibrating and sit below the header, and the wave drawing is SVG paths, not text. Why the suite stayed green: the pins assert each Text''s ink colour and the two-line geometry, never that only one line may paint over the other — sibling paint order is not observable to a render test — so the fix makes the doubled class unrepresentable (one Text) rather than pinned.
- 2026-10-24 (reopened) — The crossfade is deleted, not repaired: `QiblaSubtitle` becomes one plain Text whose copy flips on `showsCompass`, ink static `COLORS.text.sheetSubtitle`, and the donor, the absolute overlay, both ink worklets and their styles leave the tree. Argued twice: a sequential dissolve (fade the outgoing line''s ink to the face, unmount it at the fade''s end, mount the incoming line at face ink and fade it up) would keep a transition while never stacking two glyph sets, but it needs a JS-side state machine keyed off the UI-thread tween''s finish to sequence what one `withTiming` expression does today — for a 150 ms nicety on a line whose arrival is already announced by a haptic and by the whole stage swapping — and the colour crossfade has never once rendered clean on glass: 294 shipped it already overprinting, and both of the owner''s reads caught it, so no working visual is lost. The acceptance criterion''s own words rule the mechanism: exactly one instruction line at a time. The swap cannot resize the header: both sentences share one style so the line box holds its height, the header column is start-aligned and the icon end-pinned by the row''s `space-between`, so the sentence-width change (en: 158.6dp waiting, 150.4dp ready) moves nothing visible.
- 2026-10-24 (reopened) — Versioning for the reopened pass: every commit runs `git fetch origin` first and takes the next free patch above everything visible (uat is 2.4.24, so the step lands at 2.4.25 or higher), bumping `package.json`, `app.json` and `shared/whatsNew.ts` together. `android/app/build.gradle` is untracked (prebuild derives it from `app.json`); the v2 ruling''s naming of it among the bump files was corrected by the audit and stands corrected. The subject stays `fix`-typed, patch class. Code-only: the standing owner order on this ticket — a production-compiled mock build on both phones before the row returns to Awaiting Owner — stays the lead''s closing ritual; no step drives a phone, builds or installs.

