## Goal

The README''s content trails the app. Written once in the earliest era, it has drifted through 5,115 commits: the 1.0.x build-out (2024-10 to 2026-02), the 1.1.x/1.2.x store era (2026-01 to 2026-02), the 1.3.x-1.23 series, the 1.24-1.29 rebuild (2026-09-10 to 2026-09-27), the 2.x restructure (2026-10-11 onward) and the 2.4.x line now at 2.4.40. When this is done, every user-facing feature the history records is named in README.md grouped the way a reader wants, every claim holds against the 2.4.40 build, the survey''s per-section source list sits on this ticket, and `yarn validate` is green.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-26: The README stays reader-first, not a version-by-version changelog. The acceptance says "grouped as a reader wants them": a reader wants today''s feature set by theme. A versioned history list in the README is the exact staleness engine this ticket tears out, and the app already carries its changelog (the What''s New modal).
- 2026-10-26: The version spine is `app.json`. `package.json` skips the 1.1.x/1.2.x store versions; `app.json` carries every store number from 1.0.0 to 2.4.40. Era boundaries are read from it.
- 2026-10-26: The two existing folding-iPhone (Duo) lines carry forward verbatim, unverified. Owner order 2026-10-21 bans all Duo work, which includes the measurements a staleness check would need; the lines are owner-settled content and this ticket changes no pixel and takes no measurement.
- 2026-10-26: Survey notes are working scratch in the worktree, deleted before the branch merges. The durable source list lands as a comment on this ticket (the acceptance names the ticket as its home), and the README itself is its own citation per the repo rule that the README is the one doc that stays.
- 2026-10-26: The rewrite keeps the current section skeleton where a reader already works (Features, Known limitations, Athan audio sources, Stack, Repository layout, Development, Testing, Release ritual, Further reading) and rewrites the content inside it; sections are added or dropped only where the history or the build says so.

## Files

- `README.md` - the one file changed.
- `app.json`, `package.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` - version bump to 2.4.41, patch, per the bump-on-every-commit rule.
- `shared/whatsNew.ts` - read only: cross-check of recent release-visible changes.
- `app/`, `widgets/`, `modules/`, `shared/i18n`, `device/` - read only: claim verification against the current tree.
- `scripts/privacy-manifest.json` terms - read only: the public-repo guard the new text must pass.

## Design

Survey, then verify, then write.

1. **Era map** (measured, not guessed): first commit 939b1f18 2024-10-26; 1.1.0 a2e85e1b 2026-01-17; 1.2.0 193e1000 2026-01-20; 1.3.x 0cd2a894 2026-02-05; 1.4.0 2bea96f8 2026-02-07 (Ramadan); 1.5.0 e0bdf885 2026-02-13; 1.6-1.23 daily series 2026-08-29 to 2026-09-09; 1.24.0 334233b0 2026-09-10 to 1.29.x 2026-09-27; 2.0.0 bd5d89fa 2026-10-11; 2.1.0 2026-10-19; 2.2.0 2026-10-20; 2.3.0 b7334ed0 2026-10-20; 2.4.0 b2b703c5 2026-10-21; tip 2.4.40 dc269768 2026-10-25.
2. **The walk per era**: unique commit subjects (`git log --format=''%s'' <range> | sort -u`). Era A (1.0-1.2, 203 unique), Era B (1.3-1.23, 192) and Era E (2.4, 146) are read whole. Era C (1.24-1.29, 1,680) and Era D (2.0-2.3, 1,322) get a user-facing keyword pass (`widget|qibla|overlay|countdown|schedule|notif|athan|remind|locale|language|hijri|dark|prayer|extra|midnight|suhoor|duha|istijaba|friday|ramadan|offline|mmkv|settings|font|seconds|decoration|what|lock screen|home screen|map|compass|haptic|sound|audio|channel|alarm|exact|doze|battery|permission|onboard|tooltip|badge|icon|splash|theme|color`), then every candidate feature is confirmed by reading the commit or the file it touched. Every feature claim gets its commit hash recorded.
3. **Claim verification**: every sentence of the new README names something checkable in the 2.4.40 tree - counts (`ls`/`grep` for the 32 recordings), versions (`package.json`, `app.json`), requirements (`app.json` deployment targets), behaviors (`shared/`, `device/`, `widgets/` sources), staleness of Known limitations and Upcoming (log search for the ColorOS/OxygenOS exact-alarm fix and any store release that carried it).
4. **The rewrite**: grouped by reader need - identity and links, features (prayer times and schedules, the overlay, notifications, widgets, qibla, locales and languages, settings, What''s New, offline behaviour), platforms and requirements, London-only scope and its invariants, known limitations, sources (athan audio), development and testing, the board, release ritual. Every line either verified against the tree or quoted from owner-settled content (the Duo lines).

The invariant: nothing in the README claims what the 2.4.40 tree does not carry, and no person- or device-specific value, position or place name reaches the page (public-repo rules; `yarn validate` runs the privacy scan over it).

Alternatives rejected: a versioned changelog section (staleness engine, rejected above); a minimal diff patching only stale lines (the acceptance wants the full feature set named and grouped, not spot fixes); deleting the README as an artefact (the repo rule keeps the README as its one named survivor, cited by this ticket).

## Steps

1. **Step 1: Survey eras A, B and E** (1 point, docs). Walk the unique subjects of 939b1f18^..0cd2a894 (1.0-1.2), 0cd2a894..334233b0 (1.3-1.23) and b2b703c5..dc269768 (2.4) whole; record every user-facing change with its commit hash in the survey notes.
2. **Step 2: Survey eras C and D** (1 point, docs). Keyword pass over 334233b0..bd5d89fa (1.24-1.29) and bd5d89fa..b2b703c5 (2.0-2.3), confirm each candidate by reading its commit or tree state; record with hashes. Cross-check against `shared/whatsNew.ts` and the git birth dates of `widgets/`, `modules/`, `shared/i18n`, `shared/whatsNew.ts`.
3. **Step 3: Verify every claim and rewrite README.md** (1 point, docs). Check each existing and planned claim against the 2.4.40 tree (versions, counts, requirements, behaviours, Upcoming and Known-limitations staleness); rewrite the page reader-first carrying the Duo lines verbatim.
4. **Step 4: Validate, record, bump and commit** (1 point, docs). `yarn format` then `yarn validate` green; post the per-section source list as a comment on this ticket; bump to 2.4.41 in `package.json`, `app.json` and `android/app/build.gradle`; commit on the lane branch; delete the survey scratch.

## Risks

- Era C/D keyword filter drops a feature whose subject uses no keyword (a silent miss). Shows as a feature present in the tree with no survey entry; the step-3 tree verification catches it because every README claim needs a source, and every tree feature needs a claim.
- A store release the log calls shipped did not actually reach the stores. Mitigation: store versions are claimed only from release/submit commits, and the Known-limitations line is only moved when a release commit provably carries the fix.
- The rewrite drifts into marketing prose. Mitigation: the acceptance is coverage and freshness, not voice; the AGENTS.md writing rules govern.
- The 100%-coverage Jest gate fails on an unrelated flake and reads as our regression. Mitigation: `yarn validate` runs on the base commit first to prove the suite green before any edit.

## Proof

- Coverage: the survey''s source list on the ticket maps each README section to commits or ranges; a reviewer re-runs `git log --format=''%s'' <range> | sort -u` against it.
- Freshness: every README claim names its tree evidence (file and what it shows); the reviewer spot-checks versions against `package.json`/`app.json`, the recording count against the picker source, requirements against `app.json`.
- Source list recorded: the ticket comment exists (`list_issue_activity` on T-347).
- `yarn validate` green: the command exits 0 on the lane branch tip.

**Story points: 4** (four docs steps, 1 each).', NULL, NULL, '{}', false, false, false, NULL, NULL, 36864, 1, 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', '2026-10-25 07:48:14.094704+00', '2026-10-25 07:48:14.094704+00');
INSERT INTO public.project_document (id, project_id, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, archived_by_ancestor_id, "position", version, owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, updated_by_user_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (31, 1, NULL, 'T-296', '# T-296 - The What''s New archive speaks every locale

## Goal

Today the What''s New modal renders its seven historical items in English under every non-English locale (owner report 2026-10-20: on Arabic, the language item reads Arabic and the seven after it English), and the language item''s body translates an English source that no longer exists - the owner''s 2026-10-21 copy order rewrote all eight bodies to the one-line verb-first pattern. When this is done, all eight items read translated under ar, ms, so, hi, th from the new English, the en catalog is byte-identical, and any future untranslated archive string fails the suite.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-21 - The language item''s five titles stay; only its body joins the retranslation. Each title (اللغة, Bahasa, Luqadda, भाषा, ภाषา) already translates the unchanged en title "Language"; re-translating a faithful string is churn against the shortest-words order.
- 2026-10-21 - The lock is a per-locale arm of the WHATS_NEW content contract in shared/__tests__/whatsNew.test.ts (equality with the en value fails), and shared/__tests__/catalogGates.test.ts drops its two stand-in exemptions (the echo exemption and the ar RTL skip for the seven keys) in the same change. The exemptions were the stand-ins'' only pass; leaving them would hide the exact regression the gates exist to catch.
- 2026-10-21 - Register: every body opens with the locale''s own shortest "added" participle over the harvested terminology (ar أضيف/أضيفت passive, ms Ditambah, so Waxaa lagu daray, hi जोड़ा गया, th เพิ่ม); the second-reminder body keeps the "each prayer now has" shape; ar carries the dual تنبيهان instead of a digit. Thai and Hindi word order keeps the participle where their grammar puts it - the register matches, not the English word order.
- 2026-10-21 - Length: every title sits within the 32-char hard limit (the verbose scripts land at 30-31) and every body within 96 and within roughly 2x its en length (longest: so widgets body 80 against en 42); the lock asserts the limits per locale so an over-budget edit fails before merge.
- 2026-10-21 - One commit typed fix(i18n) (the archive rendering English is the owner-reported defect), patch bump: 2.4.5 if free at commit time, decided after git fetch and a local-branch scan; a collision takes the standing second-merge-renumbers ruling recorded on rows 293/295, with the entry riding the commit in scripts/version-collisions-allowlist.json (never version-major-allowlist.json, which is the owner''s majors-only record). The red-first proof runs on the lane before the translations land - the pre-commit hook demands a green tree, so the lock and the translations share the commit.
- 2026-10-21 - Acceptance criterion 1 (the owner''s verification pass on the drafts, which the owner rules per the copy process) is the owner''s alone. The lane lands, validates, audits and merges everything else, then parks the row in Awaiting Owner naming that pass.

## Files

- shared/i18n/ar.ts - 15 values change (seven stand-in items plus the language body)
- shared/i18n/ms.ts - 15 values change
- shared/i18n/so.ts - 15 values change
- shared/i18n/hi.ts - 15 values change
- shared/i18n/th.ts - 15 values change
- shared/__tests__/whatsNew.test.ts - the per-locale content-contract arm
- shared/__tests__/catalogGates.test.ts - the two stand-in exemptions deleted
- shared/whatsNew.ts - WHATS_NEW.version moves with the bump (the disk-read oracle pins it to app.json)
- package.json, app.json, android/app/build.gradle (untracked on disk) - the version bump
- scripts/version-collisions-allowlist.json - an entry only if a sister lane holds the number when this one commits
- shared/i18n/en.ts, shared/i18n/catalog-lock.json, shared/__tests__/i18n.test.ts - read only, byte-identical

## Design

The invariant: an archive string ships translated or the suite fails. Three locks hold it after this lands:

1. The existing key-set gate (each catalog holds exactly the en key set) - untouched.
2. The new contract arm: for each of ar, ms, so, hi, th, resolve the archive through tIn(locale, key) (shared/i18n/index.ts:57, the named-locale read that mutates no global state) and fail on any title or body equal to its en value, on any empty string, and on any title over MAX_WHATS_NEW_TITLE_LENGTH (32) or body over MAX_WHATS_NEW_BODY_LENGTH (96).
3. catalogGates re-tightened: the echo rule (a value containing its en source fails) and the ar Latin rule now cover the whatsNew keys like every other key.

The drafts, from the new English source, over the harvested terminology (the full table the executors copy verbatim):

