INSERT INTO public.project_document (id, project_id, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, archived_by_ancestor_id, "position", version, owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, updated_by_user_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (38, 1, NULL, 'T-345 - the reminder segments keep English''s breathing room in every locale', '# T-345 - The reminder segments keep English''s breathing room in every locale

## Goal

Today the reminder rows'' segmented control fills the width left of a fixed 100 label column and splits it 50/50 between Silent and Sound. Each option centers its content (icon + gap + label). In Somali the labels (`Aamusan`, `Dhawaaq`) are wider than English''s, so the centered content fills the whole 50 percent share and the horizontal breathing room collapses. The other five shipped locales fit. When this is done, every locale''s widest option keeps at least the per-side padding today''s English layout shows, the control grows leftward into the label column by exactly the excess, and English (and every locale narrower than English) renders the pixels it renders today.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-25 - The floor is the English pair''s slack measured at runtime at the live row geometry (English strings in English typography), not a static dp constant. Why: "exactly the padding today''s English layout shows" and "English''s own layout unchanged" both hold by construction at every device width; any constant breaks one or the other (English''s real slack varies with screen width).
- 2026-10-25 - The growth mechanism is a shared `minWidth` host View in both rows plus `flexShrink: 1` on the label; `SegmentedControl.tsx` and `Stepper.tsx` stay byte-identical. Why: the alert sheet''s at-time control shares those components, and hosts confine the change to the reminder rows while flexbox keeps both rows equal natively. The ticket names SegmentedControl.tsx as the surface whose 50/50 behavior must hold, and it holds untouched.
- 2026-10-25 - The before row grows only to match the sound row. Why: the acceptance''s floor belongs to the segments; the stepper''s `space-between` content has no padding concept and fits inside every shipped locale''s width.
- 2026-10-25 - No wrap guard (`numberOfLines`) on the shrunken label column. Why: the owner owns testing the "no shipped language''s row approaches the Sound title" assumption as languages are added; a guard would be invented policy.
- 2026-10-25 - The first frame renders today''s layout; the measured minimum lands on the first layout callback. Why: the pill in the same control already renders only after `onLayout` (`containerWidth > 0`), and no synchronous text measure exists on the new architecture.
- 2026-10-25 - The dead `optionRow`/`optionLabel` styles in Alert.tsx stay. Why: unrelated cleanup belongs to its own ticket.
- 2026-10-25 (audit) - The measurer carries `accessibilityElementsHidden` and `importantForAccessibility: ''no-hide-descendants''`. Why: the audit found TalkBack focuses alpha-0 text, so the hidden measurer read four phantom labels per card; hiding from screen readers is part of being a measurer. Audit correction at 2.4.43.
- 2026-10-25 (audit) - The plan''s worked example "content 73, baseline 61 -> 219" was an arithmetic slip; the formula gives 215 and the suite asserts the formula. Recorded by the executor, confirmed by the audit.

The static-constant alternative was argued twice and rejected both times: a constant above English''s slack changes English on some device, a constant below under-delivers the floor, and neither is "exactly the padding today''s English layout shows".

## Files

- `components/sheets/parts/reminderRowLayout.ts` - new pure module: the row furniture constants, the content-width helper, and `requiredControlWidth`.
- `components/sheets/parts/__tests__/reminderRowLayout.test.ts` - new suite: red before green, then the mutation pass on the guards.
- `components/sheets/screens/ReminderCard.tsx` - the hidden measurers, the row `onLayout`, the shared `minWidth` hosts, `flexShrink` on the label.
- `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/ReminderCard.test.tsx` - new suite: six locales, both rows equal, English unchanged.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `shared/whatsNew.ts` - the patch version bump each commit carries (2.4.41, 2.4.42, then the audit correction''s 2.4.43). `android/` is untracked prebuild output in this repo, so no commit can carry `android/app/build.gradle`; app.json plus prebuild is the real path, and both commits follow it.
- `scripts/version-collisions-allowlist.json` - the entries recording the 2.4.41 and 2.4.42 stamps this lane shares with lanes T-327 and T-347 under the standing collision ruling.
- `components/sheets/parts/SegmentedControl.tsx`, `components/sheets/parts/Stepper.tsx`, `components/sheets/screens/Alert.tsx` - read, proven untouched.

## Design

The invariant: a reminder row''s control width is `max(availableWidth, requiredControlWidth)`, and the label column yields only the excess. The algebra, with `available = rowWidth - 100 - SPACING.md` (the label column and the row gap) and `optionToday = (available - 6) / 2` (the wash container''s 3pt padding each side):

```
floor            = max(0, optionToday - baselineContent) / 2
requiredControl  = (activeContent + 2 * floor) * 2 + 6
```

`baselineContent` and `activeContent` are each the wider of the pair''s two options: icon 13 + gap `SPACING.sm` + measured label text width. The first is the English pair measured in English typography (`typographyFor(''en'')`); the second is the active pair in the active typography. When the floor is positive the algebra collapses to `requiredControl - available = 2 * max(0, activeContent - baselineContent)`: the control grows by exactly twice the content''s excess, each option grows by the excess, and the active pair''s widest option then carries a per-side slack of exactly `floor`. English has `activeContent == baselineContent`, so its `requiredControl` equals its available width exactly: the minimum binds at equality and no pixel moves. A locale narrower than English never binds. A device so narrow that English itself has no slack gets `floor = 0` and a pure content fit - the range where today''s English already overflows its option.

`requiredControlWidth` guards missing measurements (`rowWidth <= 0` or either content width `<= 0`) by returning 0, which is no minimum at all - today''s layout - until the first layout callback delivers real numbers.

In `ReminderCard`, both option rows render their control inside a host View styled `{ flexGrow: 1, minWidth: requiredControl }`; the label Text gains `flexShrink: 1` beside its fixed `width: 100`. Flexbox does the negotiation: when the minimum exceeds the available width, only the label yields, by exactly the excess, and because both rows carry the same minimum over the same geometry, both controls render equal widths with their outer edges on the card''s edge - the growth is leftward in LTR, mirrored in RTL, and both rows match. The segments stay `flexGrow: 1, flexBasis: 0` inside their container, so each option remains exactly 50 percent of the wash container''s interior and the pill math (`containerWidth` from the control''s own `onLayout`) is untouched.

Measurement: one absolutely-positioned, `opacity: 0`, `pointerEvents: ''none''` View inside the card carries four Texts - the English pair under the English typography and the active pair under the active typography - each reporting `onTextLayout`''s `lines[0].width`. The two maxima feed the pure function with the row''s measured width. The layout root already remounts on a locale switch (`localeVersionAtom`), so the accumulated maxima reset with the locale.

Alternatives rejected: a static floor constant (breaks exactness or English, above); capping growth at the label''s own text width (invented policy the owner reserved); measuring inside SegmentedControl and calling back (splits the row''s furniture across files - the label column is ReminderCard''s style); per-locale width tables (the ticket bans language-specific rules).

## Steps

1. **Step 1: the reminder-row layout math and its suite (2 points)** - `reminderRowLayout.ts` with `segmentContentWidth` and `requiredControlWidth` plus the constants, and `reminderRowLayout.test.ts` proving: the content helper, English''s required equal to available, growth exactly twice the content excess, the resulting slack equal to the floor when growing and above it when not, the zero floor on degenerate-narrow geometry, and 0 for every missing measurement. Red before green, then a mutation pass: remove the floor''s `max(0, ...)` and each guard and watch the named tests fail. Version bump 2.4.41.
2. **Step 2: the measured floor wired into the reminder rows and its suite (2 points)** - the measurers, the row `onLayout`, the shared `minWidth` hosts and `flexShrink` label in `ReminderCard.tsx`, and `ReminderCard.test.tsx` driving `onTextLayout`/`onLayout` under all six shipped locales: both hosts always carry the same `minWidth`, Somali''s grows by exactly twice the excess, English''s equals its available width with the label''s `width: 100` intact, narrower locales never bind, and the resulting per-side slack is at least the floor in every locale - asserted numerically. `Alert.test.tsx` and `SegmentedControl.test.tsx` stay green untouched. `yarn validate` green. Version bump 2.4.42.

## Risks

- The first frame shows today''s layout and the minimum lands on the first layout callback, visible as one reflow under Somali only. The same control''s pill already renders only after `onLayout`; if the owner rules the reflow a defect, a native synchronous text measure is the fallback and is out of scope here.
- A future language wider than English by more than the label column can yield would wrap its title text (no `numberOfLines` guard, by decision above).
- `fireEvent(el, ''textLayout'', ...)` has no precedent in this suite; if the harness rejects the event name, the tests call the handler through the element''s props, the way the pill''s geometry tests already drive `layout`.
- Jest coverage thresholds apply to the two new files; every new line is exercised by the suites above.

## Proof

- Floor per locale, measured: `npx jest reminderRowLayout ReminderCard` - the six-locale cases assert `((minWidth - 6) / 2) - activeContent >= floor` numerically, equality when growth is positive.
- 50 percent each, equal pair, equal rows: `npx jest SegmentedControl ReminderCard` - the untouched pill tests still pass one segment wide; both hosts assert the same `minWidth`; the label keeps `width: 100`.
- Minimum growth, English unchanged, no maximum: `npx jest reminderRowLayout` - English''s required equals available exactly; growth equals twice the content excess exactly; no cap exists in the function.
- `yarn validate` green: `tsc --noEmit && biome check . --error-on-warnings && jest --silent --coverage`.
