INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (65, 24, 1, NULL, 'T-276', '# T-276 — Ten bottom-bar arrangements, screenshotted for the owner''s pick

Owner order 2026-10-20. The deliverable is ten screenshots on this row, not merged code: the branch dies after the shots, uat never moves.

## The three elements (unchanged primitives)

The real SettingsButton (43px wide, the real colors, border, shadow, haptics) and the two real 6px schedule dots (Standard/Extra, active/inactive opacity). Every design rearranges only their container. Real mock data behind them (mock build: prayers sit either side of launch).

## The ten designs

1. **One Line (the owner''s fixed spec)** — the button''s bottom edge sits on the line the dots'' bottoms sit on today, clear of the home indicator; the dots flank it left and right, all three vertically centred on that one line: small dot, big button, small dot.
2. **Corner Pair Left** — button bottom-left corner, dots side-by-side bottom-right. Mirrored asymmetry; frees the whole bottom centre. Trade: the dots sit far from the button they orbit.
3. **Corner Pair Right** — the mirror of 2: button bottom-right, dots bottom-left. Same trade, other thumb.
4. **Floating Pill** — one frosted pill centred on the line, holding dot, button, dot inside it. Trade: reads as a single control; the pill adds its own visual weight.
5. **Integrated Capsule** — the button widens into a capsule and the two dots dock inside its left and right ends. Trade: smallest footprint of all; the dots stop reading as pages to some eyes.
6. **Edge Rail Right** — vertical stack pinned to the right edge: button on top, the two dots below it stacked vertically. Trade: the bottom centre is fully clear; dots read top-to-bottom as pages.
7. **Edge Rail Left** — the mirror of 6 on the left edge.
8. **Segmented Track** — a full-width hairline track near the bottom; the button centred on it, one dot at each end. Trade: maximal symmetry; the track anchors the whole screen foot.
9. **Wide Aperture** — button centred on the line, the two dots pushed out near the screen''s side edges at the same height. Trade: the most air; the dots all but vanish until swiped.
10. **Corner Stack** — button bottom-left, the two dots stacked vertically bottom-right. Trade: diagonal balance, the vertical pair doubles as a page ladder; the busiest of the four corner designs.

## Switcher mechanics (debug-only, branch-only)

- Gate: `EXPO_PUBLIC_DESIGN_SWITCHER=1` at build time. Any build without the env renders today''s shipped layout through a byte-identical path: the gate is the default-off branch.
- A debug overlay in the Navigation chrome layer: an invisible full-width tap strip across the top of the screen; each tap advances the design 1 to 10 and wraps. A tiny `Dn/10` badge (top corner, 10px, low opacity) so every screenshot self-identifies from its pixels.
- No test coverage demanded (throwaway); `yarn validate` stays green so the build works.

## Shot list

- Worktree `$HOME/athan-gitree/worktrees/lane-276`, branch `lane/276` off uat 2.1.33. Author Athan. Never pushed, never merged, deleted at the close.
- No other build may run at once (the Duo lane builds nothing this run; checked before start).
- Mock iOS Release build of the branch with the switcher env, installed on the physical iPhone XS (`IPHONE_UDID`). One throwaway launch after install (What''s New), then per design: tap strip, settle, screenshot, ten times.
- `design-01.png` through `design-10.png` attached to this row in order, one comment per design naming what varies and what it trades. Screenshots never commit to the repository.

## Steps

- Step 1 (code, 2 pts): the switcher and the ten arrangements land on `lane/276`, validate green, version bump per commit.
- Step 2 (device, 3 pts): mock build on the iPhone XS, the ten screenshots attached in order with their comments.

## Audit

Two reviewers on the protocol''s honesty: the shots match the designs, nothing leaked (no screenshots in the repo, no device identifiers outside placeholders), nothing merged. Not code quality of a throwaway.

## Risks

- A dropped tap desynchronises shot order: the badge on every shot makes desync visible from pixels; a mismatched shot is retaken.
- Metro env-blindness: the build runs with a fresh TMPDIR so no stale transform ships without the switcher.
- iOS build time and signing are the long poles; nothing else runs beside them.', NULL, 'compass', '{}', false, false, false, NULL, 23552, 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', '2026-10-20 03:54:08.519408+00');
