INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (99, 35, 1, NULL, 'T-327', '# T-327

## Goal

The 3T fell below the animation floor it held: the prayer overlay opens janked (the worst of it), the alert and settings sheets drag, while the iPhone XS stays smooth. The owner''s memory: 60fps everywhere, 30 the minimum. Done means: a Release gate-ON build on the 3T passes the 30fps floor (frame gaps at most 33ms, no multi-frame freezes, 16-17ms cadence the target) on the overlay''s open and close and both sheets'' entrances, the regressing commits are named by measurement, the root cause is named with frame evidence, and the iPhone XS measures unchanged before and after.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 D1: measure the uat tip before any bisect. The baselines date to the 2026-09-11/12 re-bases; nothing between then and 2.4.24 has been measured on the 3T, so the tip''s numbers come first and every later comparison hangs off them.
- 2026-10-24 D2: frame evidence is the verdict, marks are triage. The overlay_open band moved with the s9 useLayoutEffect instrument (e2e/baselines/android-3t.json, _2026_09_11: "compare builds with frame evidence, not this mark"), and the acceptance criteria are floors, not marks.
- 2026-10-24 D3: bisect anchors. 5b496afe (2.4.11, last uat before 294''s lane work), f97cd7d4 (2.4.17, 294 merged), 887d7949 (2.4.23, 322 merged), tip 1c22014c (2.4.24). If the pre-294 anchor is already regressed, the window widens backwards over uat''s first-parent history with the same halving loop, and the plan continues from wherever the clean anchor lands.
- 2026-10-24 D4: the XS is measured with the in-app marks instrument before and after (PERF_MEASURE over pymobiledevice3 syslog live, tag Athan{React}, a Release configuration build driven by agent-device), plus the owner''s eyeball on the same builds. Maestro cannot drive physical iOS and the harness has no iOS frame instrument, so marks plus eyeball are what iOS can honestly produce. "Unchanged" means each interaction''s after-median sits inside the band the before-run''s own spread shows, judged only after two runs of the same build establish that spread.
- 2026-10-24 D5: the fix preserves 294''s pinned invariant. No text renders through opacity; text inks paint alpha exactly 0 or 1 (the text-ink sweep inside yarn validate enforces it). A fix that restores opacity fades on text is not a candidate.
- 2026-10-24 D6: every measurement build is Release gate-ON, dev env, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1 (shared/perf.ts folds marks out when EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod, so a prod build can never emit them), serialized through the single build slot: never two builds at once, never beside a build-prod or build-mock run. All builds share the dev env, so deltas across them are valid and absolute startup numbers never compare to production.
- 2026-10-24 D7: version. Each executor fetches origin first and takes the next free patch above every version visible on the refs and the board (uat sits at 2.4.24, so the first takes 2.4.25 unless the fetch shows higher), bumping package.json, app.json and android/app/build.gradle together.

## Files

Read:
- e2e/README.md - mandatory before any measurement; its Gotchas section is the trap list
- e2e/AGENTS.md - loads on touching e2e files
- e2e/baselines/android-3t.json - the comparison baselines and the floor verdicts
- e2e/scripts/baseline-compare.sh - mark medians against the baselines
- e2e/scripts/frame-audit.sh - per-frame compositor truth and the vision prompt
- e2e/flows/overlay-x10.yaml and e2e/flows/sheets-x10.yaml - the two drives
- e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md - read before any screen work on the 3T
- e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md - the XS build, install and drive mechanics
- hooks/useAnimation.ts - the veil and ink hooks (hypothesis H1)
- components/prayer/Prayer.tsx, Time.tsx, Alert.tsx, Ago.tsx - the per-row veil wiring (H1, H2)
- components/overlay/OverlayInfoBox.tsx and components/prayer/Explanation.tsx - the info box decomposition (H3)
- components/sheets/parts/Sheet.tsx and the alert and settings sheet screens - the sheet entrance path (H4)
- stores/atoms/overlay.ts - the per-row derived atoms that fan one overlay write out to every row

Changed, only where the measurement sends the fix:
- the suspect file the bisect names, with red-first coverage beside it
- e2e/baselines/android-3t.json - medians and floors re-based with a dated note
- e2e/README.md - only when the investigation learned a new trap
- package.json, app.json, android/app/build.gradle - the version bump per D7

## Design

Measurement first, conclusion second. The owner''s suspicion (ticket 294''s colour conversion era) is a hypothesis; the bisect owns the truth. The 3T (2017, SD820) is the floor device and the only measurement witness. The XS (2018, A12) is the control that must not move. The AVD is smoke-only and never a witness.

Hypotheses, named to be tested, not concluded:
- H1 (294, e3d3bf9d) the per-row veiled ink. Each row element carries useDerivedVeiledColor: two useDerivedProgress values plus an animated style whose worklet runs a nested interpolateColor (an inner interpolation between two hex strings inside an outer one) every frame, every element. An overlay open on the Standard list runs this on every hidden row''s name, digits and colon (five rows), plus the ago badge''s two hooks and the bell''s fill: dozens of concurrent per-frame colour interpolations on the UI thread. The XS absorbs that work; an SD820 may not.
- H2 (294, e3d3bf9d and b234c995) the hold-then-hide timers. Each hidden row''s hiddenSettled setTimeout fires ANIMATION_DURATION after the open and commits display:none through a JS re-render, landing inside the overlay entrance''s own frames; the ago badge and the info box add their own timers.
- H3 (294, 4249bade) per-state colour map lookups that entered render on the sheet paths: the alert sheet''s reminder cards ride per-state colour tables resolved per render.
- H4 (322, e7993f59) the sheets: the header labels'' new ink tweens (Day''s location, Countdown''s prayer name) ride the same derived machinery, and the colour modal''s pre-composited backdrop changed what every sheet entrance composites. The alpha-0 sweep is build-time validation and cannot regress runtime, so reading exonerates it.
- H5 anything else inside the window the anchors name. The list above is where the evidence points first, not what it concludes.

Fix candidates, chosen only after the cause is named, each preserving D5 and the repo''s visual settlement (fixes change behaviour, not pixels; animated components first-frame in their settled state; only value changes animate):
- one veil progress per row shared by all its ink styles, replacing two derived values per element
- hoisted or pre-parsed colour inputs to interpolateColor
- memoised per-state colour resolution off the render path
- the display:none drop batched after every fade has settled

Alternatives rejected:
- Reverting the veil to opacity fades: violates the pinned solid-ink invariant and reddens yarn validate (D5).
- Concluding from code reading: the dictation itself says the investigation owns the truth; the 3T''s history (the phantom Choreographer loop, the mock confounds) has produced false attributions before, and the baselines predate the whole window.
- Measuring on the emulator: banned by the harness; every perf number names a physical device.
- Measuring on debug or prod builds: debug cadence is meaningless and prod folds the marks out (D6).

## Steps

Points: 1 docs, 2 code, 3 device. Every device step runs alone in a fresh session, one device at a time. Every build goes through the single slot (D6). e2e/README.md is re-read before every measurement step; e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md before any 3T screen work.

1. Step 1: the tip''s numbers on the 3T (3 points, device). Build Release gate-ON at origin/uat tip (1c22014c) per e2e/README.md''s build block: clear the Metro cache and the generated bundle, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1, install with adb install -r (aapt2 badging check before, the User 0 assert after, the versionName check before measuring). Discard the first post-install launch. Verify PERF_MEASURE lines flow (adb logcat -s ReactNativeJS) before driving anything. Run baseline-compare.sh on overlay-x10.yaml and sheets-x10.yaml. Frame-audit overlay-open (tap 540 974), overlay-close (drive the open first, wait past the entrance, then record while tapping the closing row at 540 1100, the same mechanics with a two-tap drive), sheet-alert-open (979 974) and sheet-settings-open (540 1730): the video path with the vision subagent reading each contact sheet, FRAME_AUDIT=sf only as the labelled fallback. Produces: which marks regressed against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json and which floors fail, with the evidence dirs recorded.
2. Step 2: the XS before-picture (3 points, device). The same tip as a Release configuration build with EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1 per e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md. Drive ten iterations of each of the four interactions through agent-device; capture PERF_MEASURE through pymobiledevice3 syslog live (tag Athan{React}); run the capture twice to establish each mark''s spread. Produces: the four before-medians and their band, the line "unchanged" is judged against. The owner''s eyeball rides the same build.
3. Step 3: the anchor bisect on the 3T (3 points, device). Measure f97cd7d4 (294 merged) first, the owner''s suspicion. Regressed: measure 5b496afe next; still regressed there widens the loop backwards (D3), clean there puts the window at 5b496afe..f97cd7d4. Clean at f97cd7d4: measure 887d7949 (322 merged); the window becomes f97cd7d4..887d7949. Per anchor: worktree at the commit, yarn install, the same build ritual, adb install -r (add -d if the candidate ever predates the installed build''s versionCode; the code is flat 1000000 across this window), discard the first launch, baseline-compare both flows, frame-audit the interactions Step 1 named failing. Produces: the ticket window that owns the regression.
4. Step 4: the commit bisect on the 3T (3 points, device). Halve the owning window''s commits; per candidate, build and install the same way, discard the first launch, then the failing audits and marks only. Produces: the regressing commit or commits named by measurement, with each candidate''s numbers.
5. Step 5: the root cause named and the fix implemented (2 points, code). Name the cause with frame evidence: what work entered the tap path or the animation frame, on which thread (ReactNativeJS versus native in the logcat, the SF gaps in the audits), from which change (the commit the bisect named, read against the hypothesis list). Implement the fix under D5 and the visual settlement, red-first coverage on every line touched, a mutation pass on guarded logic, yarn validate green. Produces: the fix commits on the lane branch.
6. Step 6: post-fix proof on the 3T and the baselines refreshed (3 points, device). Release gate-ON build of the fix; the four frame audits pass the 30fps floor, zero gaps over 33ms with 16-17ms cadence the target, vision-read contact sheets; the marks sit inside the baseline band. Re-base e2e/baselines/android-3t.json''s medians and floors with a dated note; overlay_close_steady''s UNPROVEN verdict gets its corrected run here. Produces: the passing audits and the refreshed baselines.
7. Step 7: the XS after-picture (3 points, device). The same fix build and the same drive as Step 2, both capture runs. Produces: the four after-medians inside Step 2''s band, read side by side, and the owner''s eyeball on the same build.
8. Step 8: close-out on the final branch (2 points, code). yarn validate green on the final branch; e2e/README.md''s Gotchas gains any trap the investigation learned, only when one was learned; the version bumped per D7; the ticket''s records complete. Produces: the finished branch ready for audit.

22 points total: two code steps, six device steps.

## Risks

- The regression does not reproduce on the harness build: the phone''s state differs (a Dual Messenger parallel copy, a stale Android Studio screen-sharing agent burning CPU, thermal state). Step 1 measuring clean shows it. Then check top for app_process screensharing agents and the dumpsys package user list before any code conclusion, and report rather than bisect.
- Video capture wedges on the 3T (known since s6): a reboot restores it; FRAME_AUDIT=sf still works, but one SF run is one sample, never a verdict on its own; the video path plus a vision read stands behind any SF result recorded as a verdict.
- The bisect window widens past 294 and 322: each anchor costs one build-and-measure cycle; the loop is unchanged, only longer.
- Marks mislead: D2 keeps every verdict off the overlay_open mark; the floors are compositor truth.
- The fix trades cost for a snap: the first-frame-settled rule and the 150/200ms feel are pinned by suites, and the vision read catches a snap in Step 6''s contact sheets.
- The XS band is too loose to prove anything: two before-runs establish the spread; when the spread swamps the delta, run a third capture rather than widen the claim.
- Two builds at once: the single-slot rule (D6). A queued executor waits for the slot; a slot conflict is a stop-and-report, never a race.

## Proof

- Acceptance 1 (baseline-compare names the regressed marks, the commits identified by measurement or bisect): Step 1''s two compare.json tables against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json, and Step 4''s per-candidate tables naming the commit where the numbers flip.
- Acceptance 2 (the root cause named with frame evidence): Step 5''s record citing the failing audit''s gap list (under e2e/evidence/), the thread the work landed on (logcat tags), and the named commit''s diff.
- Acceptance 3 (overlay open and close pass the 30fps floor on a Release gate-ON build): Step 6''s frame-audit runs printing 30fps FLOOR: PASS with gaps over 33ms at NONE, vision-read.
- Acceptance 4 (the alert and settings sheets pass the same floor): Step 6''s sheet audits, the same printed verdicts.
- Acceptance 5 (the iPhone XS measurably unchanged): Step 7''s four after-medians against Step 2''s recorded band, in the ticket''s record.
- Acceptance 6 (yarn validate green): yarn validate exits 0 on the final branch, Step 8.
