INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (100, 34, 4, NULL, 'T-322', '# T-322 — A visual polish pass: the colour modal''s backdrop, the 3T''s reset ink, the header labels'' ink, the qibla sheet''s doubled instruction text, and bold platform words in Help

## Goal

Five visual defects stand on uat today: the colour modal opens with no dimming behind it, the reset control renders a black word on the 3T instead of hiding, the two header labels carry one ink in both home and overlay states, the qibla sheet''s header shows a doubled darker line while the calibration runs, and Help''s widget answer carries its platform words in the same weight as the sentence. When this ticket is done, the modal dims exactly as the other bottom sheets do, the reset hides in ink that no platform renders black, each header label carries its tuned home ink and its tuned overlay ink, the qibla header shows exactly one instruction line, and the platform words read bold in all six shipped locales. The owner reads every item on glass; the lane ships code, tests and a green `yarn validate`, nothing else.

Planned against uat f97cd7d4 (2.4.17), which carries ticket 294''s colour-carried dim whole. The ticket''s planning note named 294''s conversion as the prime suspect for the reset ink and the doubled qibla line: verified. Both defects are `color: ''transparent''` on a Text — alpha-0 ink, which Android paints black. They are the only two alpha-0 text colours left in app/ and components/ (the settings sheet''s grabber and other named colours are opaque).

**Reopened 2026-10-24** (owner''s read on the 2.4.22 production mock build, both phones): the qibla criterion alone is unmet — the compass sheet still shows doubled instruction text, the bright ''Follow below instructions'' line with dark text stacked over it, on the iPhone as well as Android. Everything else in the pass stood approved, merged at 2.4.23. The reopened pass adds Step 5 below; Steps 1-4 shipped and their sections stand as history.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 — The two Android black-ink defects are one defect class: alpha-0 text ink. Each site stops hiding in alpha-0 ink and paints the literal face it sits on: the qibla donor paints `COLORS.surface.sheet` (#0b183a, the face its own crossfade sibling already interpolates to), and the reset paints the settings card''s face `#101d45` — the card wash `rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.06)` flattened over the sheet, rgb(16,29,69), carried as a named constant in ColorPicker.tsx beside the file''s existing flatten constants. Why two faces: the reset row sits inside the Countdown Bar card (Settings.tsx `styles.card`), so sheet-solid glyphs would print a dark word on both platforms; the donor sits on the bare sheet header, where the sheet solid is exact.
- 2026-10-24 — The text-ink sweep inside `yarn validate` is tightened to ban alpha-0 outright AND its `colourConsts` resolver is extended to bind any same-line `const` initializer, so a computed ink like `resetInk`''s ternary is visible to the check; the donor''s `color:` declaration is re-anchored (its comment moves) so `propertyValue` reaches it. Why: the griller proved the tightened sweep alone names neither site — the ternary const resolves no leaf and the comment blocks the property anchor — so the ban would be vacuous. The red run is observable: with both changes in and both sites still carrying `''transparent''`, the sweep names exactly those two.
- 2026-10-24 — The colour modal''s backdrop is `COLORS.surface.backdrop` (#000116) composited at the 0.9 the shared `renderBackdrop` passes, pre-composited as one rgba constant because the overlay View must not dim its own children. A pinning test derives the constant from `COLORS.surface.backdrop`, so the modal and the sheets cannot drift apart. Tap-outside dismissal is unchanged: the acceptance asks for the dimming alone.
- 2026-10-24 — The header labels'' tuned inks are two new `COLORS.text` roles derived from today''s shared ink #6c79c2 (h231 s41 l59) by measured shifts: home `#7485b9` (hue to 225, toward the band behind''s #031a4c at h221; saturation to 33, the blue-grey; lightness held) and overlay `#7173bc` (hue to 238, toward the glow''s #5b1eaa at h266; saturation to 36, the greyer; lightness held). Why: the owner gave direction, not values; these are one small step from today''s ink in the named directions, and the owner''s glass read is the bar. Countdown''s label rides the `overlayProgress` it already computes; Day''s location rides the `showOverlayDate` flag its masjid already rides — no new atoms.
- 2026-10-24 — Help''s bold platform words split at render time on the pinned Latin labels (`iOS: ` / `Android: `), bolding the label run in the app''s emphasis face. The six catalogs are untouched. Why: the shipped widget copy is byte-pinned with Latin labels in every locale (owner-ruled D142.11) and hash-locked; splitting at render keeps that contract and needs no lock churn.
- 2026-10-24 — Versioning: every commit runs `git fetch origin` first and takes the next free patch number above the highest it sees (uat is 2.4.17, so 2.4.18 or higher), bumping `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` and `shared/whatsNew.ts` together. Patch class throughout: no step types its subject `feat`. No prebuild, no build, no install — the owner ordered code only.
- 2026-10-24 (reopened) — Root cause ruled from the code on uat 887d7949: the subtitle''s colour crossfade paints BOTH of its lines permanently, and while the calibration runs the ready line — absolutely positioned and declared after the waiting line, so it paints over it — rests its ink at `COLORS.surface.sheet` #0b183a. That ink is invisible against the sheet face but sits directly over the waiting line''s bright #416899 glyphs, so where the two sentences'' glyphs cross, dark navy covers bright blue: glyph-shaped dark text over the bright line, both platforms, by construction (two opaque paints at one position, later declaration on top; nothing platform-specific remains). At the settled end the stack is the other way round — the bright ready line on top, the waiting line''s #0b183a beneath — where an under-paint that equals the face is invisible under every part of the upper glyphs, anti-aliased edges included, which is why the settled sheet reads clean and the calibrating sheet does not. The owner''s quoted copy settles which arm is which: ''Follow below instructions'' is `qibla.subtitleWaiting` (en.ts:133), the bright line shown while the calibration runs. The 150 ms fade between the two states stacks interpolated inks the same way, so the transition itself also reads doubled. Step 2''s donor fix was correct (the Android black ghost below the pair) but was the smaller half. The wave line is exonerated: `QiblaCalibration`''s headline and message paint #fff and #416899, mount only while calibrating and sit below the header, and the wave drawing is SVG paths, not text. Why the suite stayed green: the pins assert each Text''s ink colour and the two-line geometry, never that only one line may paint over the other — sibling paint order is not observable to a render test — so the fix makes the doubled class unrepresentable (one Text) rather than pinned.
- 2026-10-24 (reopened) — The crossfade is deleted, not repaired: `QiblaSubtitle` becomes one plain Text whose copy flips on `showsCompass`, ink static `COLORS.text.sheetSubtitle`, and the donor, the absolute overlay, both ink worklets and their styles leave the tree. Argued twice: a sequential dissolve (fade the outgoing line''s ink to the face, unmount it at the fade''s end, mount the incoming line at face ink and fade it up) would keep a transition while never stacking two glyph sets, but it needs a JS-side state machine keyed off the UI-thread tween''s finish to sequence what one `withTiming` expression does today — for a 150 ms nicety on a line whose arrival is already announced by a haptic and by the whole stage swapping — and the colour crossfade has never once rendered clean on glass: 294 shipped it already overprinting, and both of the owner''s reads caught it, so no working visual is lost. The acceptance criterion''s own words rule the mechanism: exactly one instruction line at a time. The swap cannot resize the header: both sentences share one style so the line box holds its height, the header column is start-aligned and the icon end-pinned by the row''s `space-between`, so the sentence-width change (en: 158.6dp waiting, 150.4dp ready) moves nothing visible.
- 2026-10-24 (reopened) — Versioning for the reopened pass: every commit runs `git fetch origin` first and takes the next free patch above everything visible (uat is 2.4.24, so the step lands at 2.4.25 or higher), bumping `package.json`, `app.json` and `shared/whatsNew.ts` together. `android/app/build.gradle` is untracked (prebuild derives it from `app.json`); the v2 ruling''s naming of it among the bump files was corrected by the audit and stands corrected. The subject stays `fix`-typed, patch class. Code-only: the standing owner order on this ticket — a production-compiled mock build on both phones before the row returns to Awaiting Owner — stays the lead''s closing ritual; no step drives a phone, builds or installs.

## Files

- `shared/constants.ts` — gains `surface.backdropDim` and the two `text` roles `labelHome` and `labelOverlay`.
- `components/sheets/screens/ColorPicker.tsx` — the modal overlay''s background; the reset''s hidden ink as a named card-face constant.
- `components/sheets/screens/Settings.tsx` — read only: the card wash the reset''s face derives from.
- `components/sheets/screens/Qibla.tsx` — the donor''s ink and its style''s comment anchor.
- `components/__tests__/textInk.test.ts` — the sweep bans alpha-0 text ink and resolves same-line const initializers.
- `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/ColorPicker.test.tsx`, `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/Qibla.test.tsx` — the new pins.
- `components/countdown/Countdown.tsx`, `components/day/Day.tsx` — the two labels'' inks.
- `hooks/useAnimation.ts` — `useDerivedColor`, the derived-ink hook the sweep''s `TEXT_INK_HOOKS` list already guards; it returns with two real consumers.
- `components/countdown/__tests__/Countdown.test.tsx`, `components/day/__tests__/DayLines.test.tsx` — the ink pins (Countdown.test.tsx:189''s `text.secondary` pin moves to `labelHome`).
- `shared/help.ts`, `shared/__tests__/help.test.ts` — the pure label splitter and its pins.
- `components/modals/Help.tsx`, `components/modals/__tests__/Help.test.tsx` — the bold render and its pins.
- Version files on every commit: `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle`, `shared/whatsNew.ts`.
- Reopened pass (Step 5): `components/sheets/screens/Qibla.tsx` — the subtitle becomes one Text; the donor, the absolute ready line, both ink worklets and the `subtitleDonor` and `subtitleOver` styles are deleted, with the imports the file stops using (`interpolateColor`, `useAnimatedStyle`, `useDerivedValue`, `withTiming`). `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/Qibla.test.tsx` — the crossfade pins die with the mechanism they pinned; the single-line pins land red first. `components/__tests__/typographySweep.test.tsx` — `qiblaSubtitleStyleUnder` reads the surviving `qibla-subtitle` testID. Version files on the step''s commit: `package.json`, `app.json`, `shared/whatsNew.ts`.

## Design

**The backdrop.** The colour modal is a plain RN `Modal` whose overlay View paints `transparent`. It takes `backgroundColor: COLORS.surface.backdropDim` = `rgba(0, 1, 22, 0.9)` — the channels of `COLORS.surface.backdrop` (#000116) at the 0.9 the sheets'' shared `renderBackdrop` composites. The alpha rides the colour, never the View''s `opacity`, so the modal content above it stays opaque. The test derives the expected string from `COLORS.surface.backdrop` at build time, pinning the derivation rather than the bytes.

**The hidden inks.** The reset text hides today at `color: ''transparent''` (a same-line ternary const, ColorPicker.tsx:99); on Android alpha-0 ink paints black, so the 3T shows a black reset word at default colour. The qibla subtitle''s width donor carries the same `''transparent''` behind a comment (Qibla.tsx:263). The sweep changes come first, so the fix is provably caught: its offence condition drops the 0 carve-out on every arm (static colours, ink-hook endpoints, animated interpolations), its roles test says alpha exactly 1, and `colourConsts` binds any same-line const initializer — `/const (\w+) = ([^\n]+)/` — leaving `colourLeaves` to pull the literals, COLORS paths and bound identifiers out of the expression. The donor''s comment moves above the entry or beside the value, so `propertyValue`''s `(?:^|[,{])\s*color\s*:` anchor reaches the declaration. Run `yarn validate` now: the sweep names exactly the reset''s ternary and the donor''s entry, red. Then the reset''s hidden leaf becomes `#101d45` (the card face, named `RESET_HIDDEN_INK`-style beside `labelDisabled` and `chevronDisabled`, with the derivation in its comment) and the donor''s becomes `COLORS.surface.sheet`; the sweep goes green. The reset stays mounted so the row holds its width, and its accessibility hiding stays as it is. `alphaOf`''s parser self-test keeps `transparent` returning 0: the parser must still read it to name it an offence.

**The label inks.** Two `COLORS.text` roles carry the tuned values. Each label keeps its static style colour at the home ink and interpolates to the overlay ink through `useDerivedColor`, a thin hook over `useDerivedProgress` + `interpolateColor` between two opaque solids — 294''s own pattern, sweep-checked at its endpoints, first frame settled because `useDerivedProgress` snaps on first evaluation. Countdown''s prayer name rides the `overlayProgress` its digits already ride; Day''s location rides a derived progress on `showOverlayDate` at `ANIMATION.duration`, the same flag and duration its masjid fade rides. The date line, the countdown digits and everything else keep their inks.

**The bold words.** `splitPlatformLine` in `shared/help.ts` matches a line against `/^(iOS|Android): /` and returns the label run and the remainder, or null. Help''s answer Text renders each line with the label run wrapped in a nested Text carrying `ty.familyMedium` — the emphasis face the question rows already carry, per locale. The six catalogs, the lock file and the byte-pinned copy tests are untouched; the splitter is pinned against every locale''s real catalog string.

**Alternatives rejected.** Hiding the reset by unmounting it: the row''s right side re-layouts when a colour is picked, a pixel change the owner has not ordered. Hiding by wrapper View opacity: it paints text through opacity, the exact thing 294''s sweep exists to stop. Hiding the reset against `COLORS.surface.sheet`: the card wash sits between, and sheet-solid glyphs print a dark word on both platforms — the griller''s catch. Deriving the labels'' overlay ink from the glow at runtime: the tune is a fixed pair of ruled constants, not a computation, so it stays testable as bytes. Stripping the platform prefixes out of the six catalogs and bolding code-supplied words: it fights the owner-ruled Latin-label copy contract and churns the hash lock for no gain.

**The subtitle''s one line (Step 5, reopened).** One plain Text, copy by state, no animation: it renders `qibla.subtitleWaiting` while the compass is not drawn and `qibla.subtitleReady` once it is, carrying `styles.subtitle` (static `COLORS.text.sheetSubtitle` ink) and `numberOfLines={1}`, testID `qibla-subtitle`; the component''s doc comment states the swap. The style-less wrapper `View` goes with the crossfade: the component returns the Text alone. The deleted pieces: the waiting and ready `useAnimatedStyle` worklets with their `interpolateColor` arms, the `useDerivedValue` progress, the donor Text with its `subtitleDonor` style, the `subtitleOver` style, and the now-unused imports. First frame settled by having no animation at all. The new pins, red against uat''s three-Text tree before the code lands: exactly one instruction text mounted in each state — `qibla-subtitle` present, `qibla-subtitle-donor` and `qibla-subtitle-ready` absent, no text node carrying the other state''s copy — with flattened colour `COLORS.text.sheetSubtitle` and `numberOfLines` 1; the copy pair pinned per locale over `LOCALE_IDS`, before and after the draw. The mutation proof is uat''s own shape: mounting a second instruction line reddens the exactly-one assertions. `typographySweep.test.tsx`''s `qiblaSubtitleStyleUnder` moves to the `qibla-subtitle` testID with its per-locale typography assertions unchanged.

## Steps

1. **Step 1: the colour modal carries the sheets'' dimming backdrop** (2 points). `surface.backdropDim` lands in `shared/constants.ts`; `ColorPicker.tsx`''s `modalOverlay` paints it; `ColorPicker.test.tsx` pins the overlay colour and its derivation from `COLORS.surface.backdrop` at 0.9, red first.
2. **Step 2: alpha-0 text ink leaves the tree** (2 points). The sweep drops its 0 carve-out, its roles test says alpha exactly 1, and `colourConsts` binds same-line const initializers; the donor''s comment re-anchors; watched red, the sweep names exactly the reset''s ternary and the donor''s entry; the reset''s hidden leaf becomes the card-face constant `#101d45` and the donor''s becomes `COLORS.surface.sheet`; `ColorPicker.test.tsx` pins the reset''s colour per state (`#101d45` at default, `#5b77a4` shown, `#1f3055` custom under a hidden bar) and `Qibla.test.tsx` pins the donor''s ink at the sheet solid; sweep green. The extended resolver is mutation-proven: a planted same-line const ternary carrying `''transparent''` on a Text style must redden it.
3. **Step 3: the header labels take their tuned home and overlay inks** (2 points). `text.labelHome` `#7485b9` and `text.labelOverlay` `#7173bc` land; `useDerivedColor` returns to `hooks/useAnimation.ts` with the two consumers; `Countdown.tsx` and `Day.tsx` carry it; the countdown and Day suites pin the home colour and the home-to-overlay interpolation endpoints, red first.
4. **Step 4: Help''s platform words read bold in every shipped language** (2 points). `splitPlatformLine` lands in `shared/help.ts`; `Help.tsx` bolds the label run; `help.test.ts` pins the split over all six locales'' widget answers and the null path on other answers; `Help.test.tsx` pins the emphasis face on the label runs and the regular face on the sentences, red first.
5. **Step 5: the qibla subtitle renders exactly one instruction line at a time** (2 points, reopened). The new `Qibla.test.tsx` pins land red first against uat''s three-Text tree; then `QiblaSubtitle` becomes the single Text per the Design section, the crossfade pins die with the mechanism they pinned, `typographySweep.test.tsx`''s helper moves to the surviving testID, and `yarn validate` goes green at full coverage. The commit carries its fetched-next version bump across `package.json`, `app.json` and `shared/whatsNew.ts`. No device, build or install.

Every step ends with `yarn validate` green and its own version bump. No step drives a phone, builds, installs or reads a screenshot: the owner tests every visual item on glass.

## Risks

- The tuned inks are derived, not owner-seen. They sit one measured step from today''s ink in the directions the owner named; if the glass read disagrees, a follow-up tune re-rules the two constants and nothing else moves.
- The hidden-ink-as-face rule holds while each text''s face stays what it is today: the donor on the bare sheet header, the reset on the card wash over the sheet. The per-site colour pins name both faces, so a card or sheet change that breaks either shows as a failing derivation, and the sweep holds the no-alpha-0 line.
- The extended `colourConsts` resolver reads same-line initializers only; a multi-line const object consumed by a Text style stays unseen. The two defect shapes (ternary const, commented StyleSheet entry) are both covered, and the sweep runs inside `yarn validate` at Step 2''s gate, so a surprise stops that step, not a later one.
- Two more animated styles run on the UI thread (the labels). The qibla subtitle already runs the same shape; nothing measurable is expected.
- Reopened pass: the words now swap instantly where a never-clean 150 ms crossfade stood. What shows it: the owner''s glass read of the words changing as the compass arrives; the remedy if it reads abrupt is a follow-up ticket ruling a sequential dissolve, not a reopen of this mechanism.
- The single line sizes the header column to its own sentence, so the column''s width changes with the state (en: 158.6dp to 150.4dp). Nothing visible moves — the column is start-aligned, the icon end-pinned by `space-between`, the row sits in a fixed-width sheet — and the height is one line either way. What would show a missed move: the owner''s read of the header as the compass arrives.

## Proof

- Colour modal backdrop: `ColorPicker.test.tsx` asserts the modal root''s overlay paints `COLORS.surface.backdropDim` and that the constant equals `COLORS.surface.backdrop`''s channels at 0.9. `yarn validate` green. The owner''s glass read closes it.
- Reset ink: `ColorPicker.test.tsx` asserts the reset text''s colour per state, with the card-face `#101d45` at default and never `''transparent''` in any state; the tightened sweep, with its extended resolver, refuses any alpha-0 text colour anywhere in app/ and components/. The owner''s glass read on the 3T closes it.
- Header labels: `Countdown.test.tsx` and `DayLines.test.tsx` pin `labelHome` at rest and the interpolation endpoints `labelHome` to `labelOverlay` on the overlay flag. The owner''s glass read closes both states.
- Qibla doubled line: `Qibla.test.tsx` pins the donor''s ink at `COLORS.surface.sheet`; the existing suite already pins the two-line crossfade geometry and inks; the sweep bans the alpha-0 class. The owner''s glass read closes it.
- Help bold: `help.test.ts` pins `splitPlatformLine` over each of the six locales'' `help.a.widgets` lines; `Help.test.tsx` pins the medium family on the label runs and the regular family on the sentences. The owner''s glass read closes it.
- Whole ticket: `yarn validate` green after every step, each commit carrying its fetched-next version bump across `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` and `shared/whatsNew.ts`.
- Qibla single line (reopened): `Qibla.test.tsx` asserts, per state and per locale, exactly one mounted instruction text — `qibla-subtitle` with the state''s copy, no `qibla-subtitle-donor`, no `qibla-subtitle-ready`, no node carrying the other copy — at `COLORS.text.sheetSubtitle`, one line. Red against uat before the fix (three texts mounted), green after; `yarn validate` green at full coverage; the text-ink sweep still bans alpha-0 ink tree-wide. The owner''s glass read on the production mock build closes it.
