INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (101, 35, 2, NULL, 'T-327', '# T-327

## Goal

The 3T fell below the animation floor it held: the prayer overlay opens janked (the worst of it), the alert and settings sheets drag, while the iPhone XS stays smooth. The owner''s memory: 60fps everywhere, 30 the minimum. Done means: a Release gate-ON build on the 3T passes the 30fps floor (frame gaps at most 33ms, no multi-frame freezes, 16-17ms cadence the target) on the overlay''s open and close and both sheets'' entrances, the regressing commits are named by measurement, the root cause is named with frame evidence, and the iPhone XS measures unchanged before and after.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 D1: measure the uat tip before any bisect. The baselines date to the 2026-09-11/12 re-bases; nothing between then and 2.4.24 has been measured on the 3T, so the tip''s numbers come first and every later comparison hangs off them.
- 2026-10-24 D2: frame evidence is the verdict, marks are triage. The overlay_open band moved with the s9 useLayoutEffect instrument (e2e/baselines/android-3t.json, _2026_09_11: "compare builds with frame evidence, not this mark"), and the acceptance criteria are floors, not marks. A floor pass on the video path is the printed "gaps>33ms: NONE" list plus a vision-read contact sheet; the SF branch''s PASS line is the labelled fallback and never a verdict on its own (the baseline''s _sf_latency_note: one SF run is one sample).
- 2026-10-24 D3: bisect anchors. 5b496afe (2.4.11, last uat before 294''s lane work), f97cd7d4 (2.4.17, 294 merged), 887d7949 (2.4.23, 322 merged), tip 1c22014c (2.4.24). If the pre-294 anchor is already regressed, the window widens backwards over uat''s first-parent history with the same halving loop, and the plan continues from wherever the clean anchor lands.
- 2026-10-24 D4: the XS is measured with the in-app marks instrument before and after (PERF_MEASURE over pymobiledevice3 syslog live, tag Athan{React}, a Release configuration build driven by agent-device), plus the owner''s eyeball on the same builds. Maestro cannot drive physical iOS and the harness has no iOS frame instrument, so marks plus eyeball are what iOS can honestly produce. "Unchanged" means each interaction''s after-median sits inside the band the before-run''s own spread shows, judged only after two runs of the same build establish that spread.
- 2026-10-24 D5: the fix preserves 294''s pinned invariant. No text renders through opacity; text inks paint alpha exactly 0 or 1 (the text-ink sweep inside yarn validate enforces it). A fix that restores opacity fades on text is not a candidate.
- 2026-10-24 D6: every measurement build is Release gate-ON, dev env, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1 (shared/perf.ts folds marks out when EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod, so a prod build can never emit them), serialized through the single build slot: never two builds at once, never beside a build-prod or build-mock run. All builds share the dev env, so deltas across them are valid and absolute startup numbers never compare to production.
- 2026-10-24 D7: version. Each executor fetches origin first and takes the next free patch above every version visible on the refs and the board (uat sits at 2.4.24, so the first takes 2.4.25 unless the fetch shows higher), bumping package.json, app.json and android/app/build.gradle together.
- 2026-10-24 D8: the aapt2 badging stop rule (AGENTS.md, fleettest id) governs owner-daily installs through build-prod.zsh and build-mock.zsh. Harness measurement builds assert the plain package id instead: aapt2 dump badging names "package name=''com.example.athan''" (APP_ID), and the install proceeds. Why: the harness''s own standing procedure (e2e/README.md) installs plain release builds with adb install -r on the 3T; the fleettest rule protects the owner''s daily phones, which these installs are not.

## Files

Read:
- e2e/README.md - mandatory before any measurement; its Gotchas section is the trap list
- e2e/AGENTS.md - loads on touching e2e files
- e2e/baselines/android-3t.json - the comparison baselines and the floor verdicts
- e2e/scripts/baseline-compare.sh - mark medians against the baselines
- e2e/scripts/frame-audit.sh - per-frame compositor truth and the vision prompt
- e2e/flows/overlay-x10.yaml and e2e/flows/sheets-x10.yaml - the two drives
- e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md - read before any screen work on the 3T
- e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md - the XS build, install and drive mechanics
- hooks/useAnimation.ts - the veil and ink hooks (hypothesis H1)
- components/prayer/Prayer.tsx, Time.tsx, Alert.tsx, Ago.tsx - the per-row veil wiring (H1, H2)
- components/overlay/OverlayInfoBox.tsx and components/prayer/Explanation.tsx - the info box decomposition (H3)
- components/sheets/parts/Sheet.tsx and the alert and settings sheet screens - the sheet entrance path (H4)
- stores/atoms/overlay.ts - the per-row derived atoms that fan one overlay write out to every row

Changed:
- e2e/scripts/frame-audit.sh - gains a pre-tap open mode (tap once, wait out the entrance, then record the second tap) so the overlay-close audit has a real drive; the analysis mechanics stay untouched
- e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md - gains the four Athan-app tap points Step 2 measures
- the suspect file the bisect names, with red-first coverage beside it
- e2e/baselines/android-3t.json - medians and floors re-based with a dated note
- e2e/README.md - only when the investigation learned a new trap
- package.json, app.json, android/app/build.gradle - the version bump per D7

## Design

Measurement first, conclusion second. The owner''s suspicion (ticket 294''s colour conversion era) is a hypothesis; the bisect owns the truth. The 3T (2017, SD820) is the floor device and the only measurement witness. The XS (2018, A12) is the control that must not move. The AVD is smoke-only and never a witness.

Hypotheses, named to be tested, not concluded:
- H1 (294, e3d3bf9d) the per-row veiled ink. Each row element carries useDerivedVeiledColor: two useDerivedProgress values plus an animated style whose worklet runs a nested interpolateColor (an inner interpolation between two hex strings inside an outer one) every frame, every element. An overlay open on the Standard list runs this on every hidden row''s name, digits and colon (five rows), plus the ago badge''s two hooks and the bell''s fill: dozens of concurrent per-frame colour interpolations on the UI thread. The XS absorbs that work; an SD820 may not.
- H2 (294, e3d3bf9d and b234c995) the hold-then-hide timers. Each hidden row''s hiddenSettled setTimeout fires ANIMATION_DURATION after the open and commits display:none through a JS re-render, landing inside the overlay entrance''s own frames; the ago badge and the info box add their own timers.
- H3 (294, 4249bade) per-state colour map lookups that entered render on the sheet paths: the alert sheet''s reminder cards ride per-state colour tables resolved per render.
- H4 (322, e7993f59) the sheets: the header labels'' new ink tweens (Day''s location, Countdown''s prayer name) ride the same derived machinery, and the colour modal''s pre-composited backdrop changed what every sheet entrance composites. The alpha-0 sweep is build-time validation and cannot regress runtime, so reading exonerates it.
- H5 anything else inside the window the anchors name. The list above is where the evidence points first, not what it concludes.

Fix candidates, chosen only after the cause is named, each preserving D5 and the repo''s visual settlement (fixes change behaviour, not pixels; animated components first-frame in their settled state; only value changes animate):
- one veil progress per row shared by all its ink styles, replacing two derived values per element
- hoisted or pre-parsed colour inputs to interpolateColor
- memoised per-state colour resolution off the render path
- the display:none drop batched after every fade has settled

Alternatives rejected:
- Reverting the veil to opacity fades: violates the pinned solid-ink invariant and reddens yarn validate (D5).
- Concluding from code reading: the dictation itself says the investigation owns the truth; the 3T''s history (the phantom Choreographer loop, the mock confounds) has produced false attributions before, and the baselines predate the whole window.
- Measuring on the emulator: banned by the harness; every perf number names a physical device.
- Measuring on debug or prod builds: debug cadence is meaningless and prod folds the marks out (D6).

## Steps

Points: 1 docs, 2 code, 3 device. Every device step runs alone in a fresh session, one device at a time. Every build goes through the single slot (D6). e2e/README.md is re-read before every measurement step; e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md before any 3T screen work.

1. Step 1: the tip''s numbers on the 3T (3 points, device). Build Release gate-ON at origin/uat tip (1c22014c) per e2e/README.md''s build block: clear the Metro cache and the generated bundle, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1, install with adb install -r after the badging assert of D8, then the User 0 assert and the versionName check before measuring. Discard the first post-install launch. Verify PERF_MEASURE lines flow (adb logcat -s ReactNativeJS) before driving anything. Run baseline-compare.sh on overlay-x10.yaml and sheets-x10.yaml. Frame-audit overlay-open (tap 540 974); frame-audit overlay-close through the pre-tap open mode added to e2e/scripts/frame-audit.sh (open at 540 974, wait out the entrance, then record the closing tap at 540 1100, per overlay-x10''s drive); frame-audit sheet-alert-open (979 974) and sheet-settings-open (540 1730). The video path with the vision subagent reading each contact sheet is the verdict; FRAME_AUDIT=sf only as the labelled fallback of D2. Produces: which marks regressed against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json and which floors fail, with the evidence dirs recorded.
2. Step 2: the XS before-picture (3 points, device). The same tip as a Release configuration build with EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1 per e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md. Install, then discard the first post-install launch (the What''s New gotcha is platform-neutral). First act of measurement: the atlas carries no Athan-app tap points on the XS, so measure the four tap points (a prayer row that opens the overlay, the closing row, the settings button, the alert bell) by screenshot with the vision subagent reading them, and write them into e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md; snapshots wedge on the countdown home screen, so screenshot-plus-vision is the read, never a live snapshot. Then drive ten iterations of each of the four interactions through agent-device by the recorded points; capture PERF_MEASURE through pymobiledevice3 syslog live (tag Athan{React}); run the capture twice to establish each mark''s spread. Produces: the four before-medians and their band, the line "unchanged" is judged against, plus the atlas rows. The owner''s eyeball rides the same build.
3. Step 3: the anchor bisect on the 3T (3 points, device). Measure f97cd7d4 (294 merged) first, the owner''s suspicion. Regressed: measure 5b496afe next; still regressed there widens the loop backwards (D3), clean there puts the window at 5b496afe..f97cd7d4. Clean at f97cd7d4: measure 887d7949 (322 merged); the window becomes f97cd7d4..887d7949. Per anchor: worktree at the commit, yarn install, the same build ritual and asserts as Step 1, adb install -r (add -d if the candidate ever predates the installed build''s versionCode; the code is flat 1000000 across this window), discard the first launch, baseline-compare both flows, frame-audit the interactions Step 1 named failing. Produces: the ticket window that owns the regression.
4. Step 4: the commit bisect on the 3T (3 points, device). Halve the owning window''s commits; per candidate, build and install the same way, discard the first launch, then the failing audits and marks only. Produces: the regressing commit or commits named by measurement, with each candidate''s numbers.
5. Step 5: the root cause named and the fix implemented (2 points, code). Name the cause with frame evidence: what work entered the tap path or the animation frame, on which thread (ReactNativeJS versus native in the logcat, the frame gaps in the audits), from which change (the commit the bisect named, read against the hypothesis list). Implement the fix under D5 and the visual settlement, red-first coverage on every line touched, a mutation pass on guarded logic, yarn validate green. Produces: the fix commits on the lane branch.
6. Step 6: post-fix proof on the 3T and the baselines refreshed (3 points, device). Release gate-ON build of the fix; the four frame audits pass the 30fps floor of D2''s video-path observable, zero gaps over 33ms with 16-17ms cadence the target, vision-read contact sheets; the marks sit inside the baseline band. Re-base e2e/baselines/android-3t.json''s medians and floors with a dated note; overlay_close_steady''s UNPROVEN verdict gets its corrected video-path run here. Produces: the passing audits and the refreshed baselines.
7. Step 7: the XS after-picture (3 points, device). The same fix build and the same drive as Step 2, both capture runs, first launch discarded, the atlas''s recorded points. Produces: the four after-medians inside Step 2''s band, read side by side, and the owner''s eyeball on the same build.
8. Step 8: close-out on the final branch (2 points, code). yarn validate green on the final branch; e2e/README.md''s Gotchas gains any trap the investigation learned, only when one was learned; the version bumped per D7; the ticket''s records complete. Produces: the finished branch ready for audit.

22 points total: two code steps, six device steps.

## Risks

- The regression does not reproduce on the harness build: the phone''s state differs (a Dual Messenger parallel copy, a stale Android Studio screen-sharing agent burning CPU, thermal state). Step 1 measuring clean shows it. Then check top for app_process screensharing agents and the dumpsys package user list before any code conclusion, and report rather than bisect.
- Video capture wedges on the 3T (known since s6): a reboot restores it; FRAME_AUDIT=sf still works, but one SF run is one sample, never a verdict on its own; the video path plus a vision read stands behind any SF result recorded as a verdict.
- The bisect window widens past 294 and 322: each anchor costs one build-and-measure cycle; the loop is unchanged, only longer.
- Marks mislead: D2 keeps every verdict off the overlay_open mark; the floors are compositor truth.
- The fix trades cost for a snap: the first-frame-settled rule and the 150/200ms feel are pinned by suites, and the vision read catches a snap in Step 6''s contact sheets.
- The XS band is too loose to prove anything: two before-runs establish the spread; when the spread swamps the delta, run a third capture rather than widen the claim.
- Two builds at once: the single-slot rule (D6). A queued executor waits for the slot; a slot conflict is a stop-and-report, never a race.

## Proof

- Acceptance 1 (baseline-compare names the regressed marks, the commits identified by measurement or bisect): Step 1''s two compare.json tables against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json, and Step 4''s per-candidate tables naming the commit where the numbers flip.
- Acceptance 2 (the root cause named with frame evidence): Step 5''s record citing the failing audit''s gap list (under e2e/evidence/), the thread the work landed on (logcat tags), and the named commit''s diff.
- Acceptance 3 (overlay open and close pass the 30fps floor on a Release gate-ON build): Step 6''s video-path frame audits printing "gaps>33ms: NONE", each contact sheet vision-read monotonic with no snap.
- Acceptance 4 (the alert and settings sheets pass the same floor): Step 6''s sheet audits, the same printed verdicts and vision reads.
- Acceptance 5 (the iPhone XS measurably unchanged): Step 7''s four after-medians against Step 2''s recorded band, in the ticket''s record.
- Acceptance 6 (yarn validate green): yarn validate exits 0 on the final branch, Step 8.

## Grill findings answered

- 2026-10-24, finding 1 (no PASS observable on the video path): fixed. D2 and Proof now define the pass as the printed "gaps>33ms: NONE" plus the vision-read contact sheet; the SF PASS line stays a labelled fallback.
- 2026-10-24, finding 2 (the close audit had no executable drive): fixed. frame-audit.sh gains a pre-tap open mode, authorized in Changed, and Step 1 names its use.
- 2026-10-24, finding 3 (no XS tap points, snapshots wedge): fixed. Step 2''s first act measures the four points by screenshot-plus-vision and writes them into the XS atlas; the drive replays them.
- 2026-10-24, finding 4 (first-launch discard missing on the XS): fixed. Steps 2 and 7 both discard it.
- 2026-10-24, finding 5 (badging rule contradiction): fixed. D8 scopes the fleettest stop to owner-daily installs and names the harness assert.
- 2026-10-24, finding 6 (Lane unset): already false on the board, the field write landed 2026-10-24 before the grill; the MCP read path returns fieldValues empty for every ticket including ones the snapshot proves carry values, so the lead verifies it at the phase boundary.
', NULL, NULL, '{}', false, false, false, NULL, 34816, 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', '2026-10-24 20:13:31.993258+00');
INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (103, 36, 2, NULL, 'T-337', '# T-337 - The clocks fall back at 02:00 London: everything time-related rides the real transition whole

## Goal

Tonight, 2026-10-25 02:00 Europe/London, the clocks fall back to 01:00 (BST to GMT). The owner ordered a live proof that every time the app shows, arms or stores rides the real transition whole: display times and dates on both schedules, the overlay and the home screen, the countdown, the day rollover, the notification arming, and the stored rows. The plan is done when the static suites plus tonight''s transcribed device readings prove each acceptance criterion, or name the defect they caught.

The hard clock: the crossing is at 01:00 UTC (02:00 BST). All prep finishes by 01:30 device time. The live window is 01:45-02:20 device time.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 - The crossing device is the iPhone XS (`IPHONE_UDID`, resolved by `xcrun devicectl list devices`). The OnePlus 3T belongs to Lane 2 tonight and appears only as a lead-gated extension. Why: the dispatch constraint; on iOS the readings are the screen and the notifications themselves.
- 2026-10-24 - The four reading instants are 01:55:00 BST, 02:00:00 BST (= 01:00:00 GMT, the fall-back), then +5 and +15 real minutes, which the wall clock reads as 01:05 GMT and 01:15 GMT. Why: after a fall-back there is no wall 02:05 within minutes of the crossing; the dispatch''s "02:05 and 02:15" are taken as +5/+15 real minutes past the transition, not wall labels. Ruling returned to the lead.
- 2026-10-24 - The midnight rollover (00:00 BST, Sat 24 to Sun 25 Oct) is captured live inside the prep step, two hours before the fall-back. Why: the owner''s order names the day rollover, and tonight is the one night the rollover and the fall-back share a day.
- 2026-10-24 - The prep step turns both schedules'' at-time athan bells on when off and records the prior state; the restore happens in Step 6, after Step 5''s Fajr fire. Why: restoring earlier disarms the armed Fajr alert before it fires and would stage a miss the app did not cause; the fire-on-time criterion is unobservable with bells off.
- 2026-10-24 - In-app taps on the XS run through the atlas Driver route: the `agent-device` CLI with the iOS runner prepared (`AGENT_DEVICE_IOS_TEAM_ID=<paid team> agent-device prepare ios-runner --udid $IPHONE_UDID`), which installs two runner apps on the phone, uninstalled when the night ends. Leaving the app uses terminate or the app switcher, never the banned home/bottom-edge swipes. Why: the atlas is the measured route; snapshots wedge on the countdown, so every read is a screenshot via `pymobiledevice3 developer dvt screenshot`.
- 2026-10-24 - After any bell change the app is relaunched once before 01:30. Why: the sheet-dismiss commit path reschedules, and the launch listener is the second event that puts a refused prayer right; the relaunch makes the armed state certain whichever path carried the change.
- 2026-10-24 - A mock build is ruled out for every live step. Why: it serves launch-relative times and does not ride the real transition. All builds carry EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod with the key from `~/.config/athan/.api_key` exported into the build process env only, never printed, never written.
- 2026-10-24 - The only code that changes tonight is tests. A gap test that exposes a real defect is recorded on this ticket and fixed in a follow-up ticket after the crossing. Why: fixing inside the window invalidates the proof the owner ordered.
- 2026-10-24 - Static gap coverage, each test proven able to fail by a mutation pass (flip the guarded logic, watch it fail, revert) and never reading the real clock: (a) the London calendar date inside both passes of the duplicated hour, (b) notification candidate rows with now inside the duplicated hour, (c) countdown display continuity across the transition instant. Why: the suites pin the fall-back instant mapping, the night rows and real-elapsed countdown windows, but not these three with now inside the duplicated hour.
- 2026-10-24 - Version: executors fetch origin and take the next free patch above everything visible (`lane/322b` carries 2.4.26; 2.4.27 is the expected number), bumping `package.json`, `app.json` and `android/app/build.gradle` together even for an iOS-only build. Why: the version-bump rule is per commit, not per platform.
- 2026-10-24 - The home-screen widget: Step 2''s home-screen read records whether a widget sits on the XS home screen. When one does, the +5 reading transcribes it from the home-screen screenshot; when none does, that reading is recorded absent and nothing is installed inside the window. Why: the widget rides the same stored rows the lists read; installing one at 01:50 buys no evidence and costs window time.
- 2026-10-24 - Arming evidence on iOS is the bell-state screenshots plus the notifications that fire (the window''s fire at its instant and Step 5''s Fajr); the alarm dump belongs to the 3T extension alone. Why: iOS exposes no scheduled-notification dump, and the acceptance clause is read through that substitute.

## Files

Changed:
- `shared/__tests__/time.test.ts` - gap pins: the London date in both passes of the duplicated hour; countdown display continuity across 01:00 UTC.
- `shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts` - gap pin: candidate rows and first still-due list day with now inside the duplicated hour.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` - the version bump.
- `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md` - written back when a route or trap is newly measured tonight.

Read, not changed: `e2e/README.md` and its Gotchas, `e2e/AGENTS.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md` (only on the 3T extension), `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-prod.zsh` (the prod env shape and the single-slot check), `shared/time.ts`, `shared/prayer.ts`, `shared/notifications.ts`, `stores/countdown.ts`, `stores/sync.ts`, `api/client.ts`, `api/config.ts`.

## Design

Approach: static proof first, one committed device through the whole night, findings recorded on the ticket as they happen.

What the suites already prove (verified 2026-10-24 by reading them):
- `shared/__tests__/time.test.ts` DST blocks: `createPrayerDatetime` maps pre-transition, duplicated and post-transition clock strings on 2026-10-25, choosing GMT (the later occurrence) inside the duplicated hour; spring-forward is pinned the same way.
- The autumn night rows: `getNightTimes(''2026-10-24'',''17:52'',''2026-10-25'',''05:04'')` pins Last Third at 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z, the second 01:00.
- The countdown window crossing the fallback counts the real 8.5h, not 7.5h; `getSecondsRemaining` is `max(1, ceil)`, so 0 seconds never displays.
- The London calendar date around winter and summer midnight; `yarn test:tz` runs the whole suite under four device timezones.
- `shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts`: rows arm whole, in time order, until the 64-request budget; an unreadable row is never armed.

The live proof rides the invariant the code is built on: prayer times are true UTC instants rendered through PRAYER_TIMEZONE. The fall-back changes only the wall-clock label of every reading; no instant moves. Every device reading is compared against the API''s own served values, fetched once in Step 1 with the key read straight into the process environment.

The reading instants, both labels:
- R1 = 01:55:00 BST = 00:55:00 UTC (last minutes of the FIRST 01:xx wall pass).
- R2 = 02:00:00 BST = 01:00:00 UTC, the fall-back instant (bracketed with reads at wall 01:59:55 BST and 01:00:05 GMT).
- R3 = 01:05:00 GMT = 01:05:00 UTC (+5 real minutes; SECOND 01:xx wall pass).
- R4 = 01:15:00 GMT = 01:15:00 UTC (+15 real minutes).

R1 sits in the first 01:xx pass and R3/R4 in the second: the same wall labels occur twice, and the day label, list content and countdown target must agree across both passes. That is the duplicated-hour proof.

Countdown continuity, scoped: the Standard countdown renders minutes outside the final ten minutes of its target, so its displayed remaining drops exactly five minutes from R1 to R2 and five more from R2 to R3 while its target name and the day stay fixed. The Extras countdown at R1 targets the 25 Oct list''s Last Third row, whose real instant (from the API''s Maghrib 24 Oct and Fajr 25 Oct) lands within minutes of the transition: its flip to Suhoor across R2-R4 is its own expected reading, not a continuity breach. The Last Third row sits on the 25 Oct Extras list because night rows file under the day the night leads into - reading it there at R1 is the expected state, not a list roll.

Notification reads: a notification that fires inside the window is transcribed live from its banner; the phone is locked once after R4 and the lock-screen entries transcribed then. "Backgrounded" for the overnight steps means locked with the app foregrounded - the atlas bans the home and bottom-edge swipes.

Alternatives rejected:
- Mock build for the crossing: serves launch-relative times, does not ride the real transition.
- Setting a phone''s clock by hand to fake 02:00: the owner ordered the real transition; a clock jump also breaks notification scheduling, and destructive clock work belongs to the disposable AVD, never a fleet phone.
- The AVD as crossing witness: the e2e rules name it smoke-only, never a witness.
- Fixing defects inside the window: invalidates the proof; follow-up ticket.

## Steps

1. **Step 1: The API''s real expected times recorded, then the static fall-back proof closed** - code, 2 points. Deadline 23:00 BST.
2. **Step 2: iPhone XS carrying the prod build through first sync, pre-crossing readings and the midnight rollover** - device, 3 points. 23:00-00:20 BST, hard prep end 01:30.
3. **Step 3: The crossing watch: four instants transcribed (R1-R4)** - device, 3 points. 01:45-02:20. The 3T extension runs inside this step only on the lead''s handover.
4. **Step 4: Post-crossing coherence: display and the offline stored rows** - device, 3 points. 02:20-02:50 GMT.
5. **Step 5: Fajr fires on time after the crossing** - device, 3 points. Fajr-10 to Fajr+10 GMT per Step 1''s fetched value.
6. **Step 6: Findings consolidated, bells restored, every acceptance criterion answered** - docs, 1 point. After Step 5.

Total: 15 points.

Step detail:

**Step 1** (code, 2). Fetch the expected values first, key never printed:
```sh
