INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (102, 36, 1, NULL, 'T-337', '# T-337 - The clocks fall back at 02:00 London: everything time-related rides the real transition whole

## Goal

Tonight, 2026-10-25 02:00 Europe/London, the clocks fall back to 01:00 (BST to GMT). The owner ordered a live proof that every time the app shows, arms or stores rides the real transition whole: display times and dates on both schedules, the overlay and the home screen, the countdown, the day rollover, the notification arming, and the stored rows. The plan is done when the static suites plus tonight''s transcribed device readings prove each acceptance criterion, or name the defect they caught.

The hard clock: the crossing is at 01:00 UTC (02:00 BST). All prep finishes by 01:30 device time. The live window is 01:45-02:20 device time.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 - The crossing device is the iPhone XS (`IPHONE_UDID`). The OnePlus 3T belongs to Lane 2 tonight and appears only as a lead-gated extension. Why: the dispatch constraint; on iOS the readings are the screen and the notifications themselves.
- 2026-10-24 - The four reading instants are 01:55:00 BST, 02:00:00 BST (= 01:00:00 GMT, the fall-back), then +5 and +15 real minutes, which the wall clock reads as 01:05 GMT and 01:15 GMT. Why: after a fall-back there is no wall 02:05 within minutes of the crossing; the dispatch''s "02:05 and 02:15" are taken as +5/+15 real minutes past the transition, not wall labels. Ruling returned to the lead.
- 2026-10-24 - The midnight rollover (00:00 BST, Sat 24 to Sun 25 Oct) is captured live inside the prep step, two hours before the fall-back. Why: the owner''s order names the day rollover, and tonight is the one night the rollover and the fall-back share a day.
- 2026-10-24 - The prep step turns both schedules'' at-time athan bells on when off, records the prior state, and the post step restores it. Why: the fire-on-time criterion is unobservable with bells off.
- 2026-10-24 - A mock build is ruled out for every live step. Why: it serves launch-relative times and does not ride the real transition. All builds carry EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod with the key from `~/.config/athan/.api_key` exported into the build process env only, never printed, never written.
- 2026-10-24 - The only code that changes tonight is tests. A gap test that exposes a real defect is recorded on this ticket and fixed in a follow-up ticket after the crossing. Why: fixing inside the window invalidates the proof the owner ordered.
- 2026-10-24 - Static gap coverage, red first, with the clock mocked (tests never read the real clock): (a) the London calendar date inside both passes of the duplicated hour, (b) notification candidate rows with now inside the duplicated hour, (c) countdown display continuity across the transition instant. Why: the suites pin the fall-back instant mapping, the night rows and real-elapsed countdown windows, but not these three with now inside the duplicated hour.
- 2026-10-24 - Version: executors fetch origin and take the next free patch above everything visible (`lane/322b` carries 2.4.26; 2.4.27 is the expected number), bumping `package.json`, `app.json` and `android/app/build.gradle` together even for an iOS-only build. Why: the version-bump rule is per commit, not per platform.
- 2026-10-24 - The home-screen widget is transcribed from the home-screen screenshot at the +5 reading when a widget already sits on the XS home screen; no widget is installed inside the window. Why: the widget rides the same stored rows the lists read; installing one at 01:50 buys no evidence and costs window time.

## Files

Changed:
- `shared/__tests__/time.test.ts` - gap pins: the London date in both passes of the duplicated hour; countdown display continuity across 01:00 UTC.
- `shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts` - gap pin: candidate rows and first still-due list day with now inside the duplicated hour.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` - the version bump.
- `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md` - written back when a route or trap is newly measured tonight.

Read, not changed: `e2e/README.md` and its Gotchas, `e2e/AGENTS.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md` (only on the 3T extension), `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-prod.zsh` (the prod env shape and the single-slot check), `shared/time.ts`, `shared/prayer.ts`, `shared/notifications.ts`, `stores/countdown.ts`, `stores/sync.ts`, `api/client.ts`, `api/config.ts`.

## Design

Approach: static proof first, one committed device through the whole night, findings recorded on the ticket as they happen.

What the suites already prove (verified 2026-10-24 by reading them):
- `shared/__tests__/time.test.ts` DST blocks: `createPrayerDatetime` maps pre-transition, duplicated and post-transition clock strings on 2026-10-25, choosing GMT (the later occurrence) inside the duplicated hour; spring-forward is pinned the same way.
- The autumn night rows: `getNightTimes(''2026-10-24'',''17:52'',''2026-10-25'',''05:04'')` pins Last Third at 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z, the second 01:00.
- The countdown window crossing the fallback counts the real 8.5h, not 7.5h; `getSecondsRemaining` is `max(1, ceil)`, so 0 seconds never displays.
- The London calendar date around winter and summer midnight; `yarn test:tz` runs the whole suite under four device timezones.
- `shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts`: rows arm whole, in time order, until the 64-request budget; an unreadable row is never armed.

The live proof rides the invariant the code is built on: prayer times are true UTC instants rendered through PRAYER_TIMEZONE. The fall-back changes only the wall-clock label of every reading; no instant moves. Every device reading is compared against the API''s own served values, fetched once in Step 1 with the key read straight into the process environment.

The reading instants, both labels:
- R1 = 01:55:00 BST = 00:55:00 UTC (last minutes of the FIRST 01:xx wall pass).
- R2 = 02:00:00 BST = 01:00:00 UTC, the fall-back instant (bracketed with reads at wall 01:59:55 BST and 01:00:05 GMT).
- R3 = 01:05:00 GMT = 01:05:00 UTC (+5 real minutes; SECOND 01:xx wall pass).
- R4 = 01:15:00 GMT = 01:15:00 UTC (+15 real minutes).

R1 sits in the first 01:xx pass and R3/R4 in the second: the same wall labels occur twice, and the day label, list content and countdown target must agree across both passes. That is the duplicated-hour proof.

The Extras schedule gives the window its sharpest reading: the 24 Oct night''s Last Third instant is computed from the real Maghrib 24 Oct and Fajr 25 Oct and lands within minutes of 01:00 UTC (with the suite''s illustrative 17:52/05:04 values, exactly on it). At R1 the Extras countdown is minutes from that row; its advance past it at R2-R4, and the row''s notification firing at its instant when armed, are transcribed live.

Alternatives rejected:
- Mock build for the crossing: serves launch-relative times, does not ride the real transition.
- Setting a phone''s clock by hand to fake 02:00: the owner ordered the real transition; a clock jump also breaks notification scheduling, and destructive clock work belongs to the disposable AVD, never a fleet phone.
- The AVD as crossing witness: the e2e rules name it smoke-only, never a witness.
- Fixing defects inside the window: invalidates the proof; follow-up ticket.

## Steps

1. **Step 1: Static fall-back proof closed and the API''s real expected times recorded** - code, 2 points. Deadline 23:00 BST.
2. **Step 2: iPhone XS carrying the prod build through first sync, pre-crossing readings and the midnight rollover** - device, 3 points. 23:00-00:20 BST, hard prep end 01:30.
3. **Step 3: The crossing watch: four instants transcribed (R1-R4)** - device, 3 points. 01:45-02:20. The 3T extension runs inside this step only on the lead''s handover.
4. **Step 4: Post-crossing coherence: display, arming state, offline stored rows** - device, 3 points. 02:20-02:50 GMT.
5. **Step 5: Fajr fires on time after the crossing** - device, 3 points. Fajr-10 to Fajr+10 GMT per Step 1''s fetched value.
6. **Step 6: Findings consolidated against every acceptance criterion** - docs, 1 point. After Step 5.

Total: 15 points.

Step detail:

**Step 1** (code, 2). Run `yarn test:tz`; run `yarn jest shared/__tests__/time.test.ts -t "fall" --silent` and `yarn jest shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts -t "budget" --silent`, reading the "N passed" lines per the jest gotcha. Write the three gap tests red first with jest fake timers or injected instants: (a) `getTodayDateString` at 2026-10-25T00:30:00Z (first 01:xx pass) and 2026-10-25T01:30:00Z (second pass) both return ''2026-10-25''; (b) `collectCandidateRows` / `firstStillDueListDayForPrayer` with now = 2026-10-25T01:30:00Z: a yesterday night row whose instant passed is not armed, every armed row is ordered by UTC instant; (c) `getSecondsRemaining` either side of 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z decreases one second per real second and never returns 0 before the target. Then fetch the expected values, key never printed:
```sh
curl -s "https://www.londonprayertimes.com/api/times?format=json&key=$(tr -d '' \n\r'' < ~/.config/athan/.api_key)&year=2026&24hours=true"
```
Transcribe into a ticket comment: the six times for 24, 25 and 26 Oct; the Extras Midnight and Last Third instants for the 24-25 night; Fajr 25 Oct in GMT (the Step 5 time-box); the expected countdown target at R1 for both schedules. `yarn validate` green. No production code changes.

**Step 2** (device, 3). Version bump per the decision above. Build the iOS prod Release per the atlas "Device build" and "Device build-only" rows: prebuild, `EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod`, `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY` from the key file into the process env only, `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` inline, xcodebuild for a device artifact, `xcrun devicectl device install app` on `IPHONE_UDID`. The iOS build precedes any 3T build tonight (`build-prod.zsh` refuses to start beside an xcodebuild, and the slot rule is never two at once). Launch once, compare the screen against Step 1''s transcription to prove real times served and stored, leave it foregrounded to finish sync and arming. Read the bell state; enable both schedules'' at-time athans when off, prior state recorded. Pre-crossing readings 23:45-23:59 BST: both schedules'' full lists and day labels, both countdown targets, the home screen, the overlay. Midnight rollover: reads at 23:58 and 00:03 BST transcribing the day label move Sat 24 to Sun 25 on both schedules, the Standard countdown target moving to Fajr, the lists swapping days. All reads are screenshots (snapshots wedge on the countdown); the atlas''s traps section governs.

**Step 3** (device, 3). Session opens 01:45, app foregrounded on the Standard page. At R1, R2 (bracketed), R3, R4 transcribe from screenshots: wall clock and UTC; countdown target name and remaining on both schedules; day label on both schedules; both schedules'' row lists; the overlay at R1 and R4; the home screen at R3 when a widget sits on it; every notification that fires in the window with its lock-screen timestamp (the Last Third row of the 24 Oct night may fire near R2 when armed - transcribe it; expected otherwise none before Fajr). The countdown must not stall or jump: R1 to R2 and R2 to R3 each consume 300 real seconds. The day label and list content at R3/R4 must equal the first pass''s. Comment the transcription on the ticket before the session ends. 3T extension, only on the lead''s handover before 23:45, sequenced after the iOS build: `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-prod.zsh <ref> <out.apk>`, install on `3T_SERIAL`, assert User 0 alone per the repo command, read `e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md` first, then the same four instants from the 3T screen plus `yarn check:device 3T_SERIAL "$APP_ID" <expected-times.json>` alarm dumps at R1 and R4 with trigger times checked against Step 1''s transcription.

**Step 4** (device, 3). Foreground the app: day label Sun 25 Oct on both schedules, lists equal to Step 1''s transcription, countdown targeting the day''s next prayer. Airplane mode on, relaunch: the stored rows alone serve the same day offline (the offline invariant is the stored-rows proof on iOS), lists identical to the online read; airplane off after. Transcribe the day''s remaining prayers displaying. Restore the bell state changed in Step 2. Transcribe the 3T''s post-crossing alarm dump when the extension ran.

**Step 5** (device, 3). From Fajr-10 to Fajr+10 GMT (Step 1''s value). Lock the phone with the side button (the XS never auto-locks while tethered; manual lock works), app in the background. Transcribe the Fajr athan notification and its lock-screen timestamp, compared against the API''s Fajr. Unlock, foreground, transcribe the countdown target advancing past Fajr. This step is the fire-on-time proof; when nothing fires, transcribe the phone''s notification settings state for the app and record the criterion unproven on iOS, with the 3T alarm dump as the fallback evidence when the extension ran.

**Step 6** (docs, 1). One comment per acceptance criterion naming its evidence: suite output lines, the Step 1 transcription, the rollover, R1-R4, the post reads, the Fajr fire. Verdict per criterion; every defect named with its follow-up ticket reference. `yarn validate` re-run when anything changed after Step 1.

## Risks

- The iOS build overruns 01:30: the crossing is then watched on whatever prod build the XS already carries, its build identity recorded from Settings; when the installed build is mock or unknown, the live criteria are recorded partial and the static proof carries the ticket. No clock is ever set by hand.
- A gap test exposes a real defect: recorded, follow-up ticket, no fix inside the window.
- Lane 2 contention on the Mac or the 3T: the optional path does not run; the iPhone path never waits on it.
- The XS arrives with a stale dev-cache: a previous mock build''s rows live in `athan-storage-dev` and are never read by a prod build; the Step 2 screen comparison proves the prod store served real values.
- The Last Third notification is not armed (bell off before Step 2, or the budget spent elsewhere): the fire evidence rests on Step 5''s Fajr.
- A reading is missed at an instant: the screenshot timestamps and the ticket comment carry what was caught; the window is not extended past 02:20.

## Proof

- Static suites on the tip: `yarn test:tz` green; `yarn jest shared/__tests__/time.test.ts -t "fall" --silent` and the notifications budget filter each report "N passed" with N > 0; the three gap tests land red first, then green, committed with the run transcripts in the ticket.
- Before the crossing: the Step 1 curl transcription equals the XS screen read in Step 2 (both schedules, both countdowns, day labels); the build report lines and the install output recorded.
- Through the crossing: the Step 3 comment carries four timestamped reading sets; countdown deltas of 300 real seconds R1-R2 and R2-R3; identical day label and list content across the two 01:xx passes; every firing notification transcribed.
- After the crossing: the Step 4 comment carries the online read, the airplane-mode relaunch read, and the remaining prayers; the 3T alarm dump shows every remaining prayer armed at its true local time when the extension ran.
- Fire on time: the Step 5 comment carries the Fajr notification transcript against the API''s Fajr value.
- Gates: `yarn validate` green in Step 1 and re-run in Step 6; all findings recorded on this ticket as they happen.
