INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (119, 42, 1, NULL, 'T-376', '# T-376: the update check on demand

## Goal

Today the app checks for updates once per launch, 1.5 seconds in, throttled by a 24-hour stamp, and the user has no way to ask again. When this is done, the settings sheet''s Other card carries a Check for updates button that runs the app''s ONE update flow on demand: the same `device/updates.ts` machinery, the same update modal, the same Play flow. The button is a second entry point, not a second pipeline. The automatic launch check and its throttle behave exactly as before. The only new surface is the inline up-to-date answer, because the update modal has nothing to show when the install is current.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-26: `checkForUpdates` takes `{ manual?: boolean }` and returns `{ modal: boolean; upToDate: boolean }` instead of a bare boolean. The manual caller must tell "the store answered: no update" apart from silence, and the automatic caller reads `.modal` alone, so its behaviour is unchanged. Rejected: a boolean plus a second manual-only wrapper, because that duplicates the pipeline the ticket forbids.
- 2026-10-26: `startNativeUpdate` returns `{ answered: boolean; updateAvailable: boolean }`. Play answering with an update (flexible flow started) must not read as up to date; the old boolean could not say.
- 2026-10-26: manual mode skips the 24-hour `popup_update_last_check` read for that call alone; the stamp writes on success and on failure exactly as the automatic check does, so the automatic check never double-fires the same window.
- 2026-10-26: no rate limit on the button beyond what a tap costs. Owner ruling 2026-10-26: the lookup endpoint is public.
- 2026-10-26: the row sits last in the Other card, after Help. Every existing row keeps its place.
- 2026-10-26: the badge is the existing check glyph (`assets/icons/svg/check.svg`, imported directly the way the What''s New row imports info-bare). No new pixel is authored, and the enum/record stays untouched.
- 2026-10-26: the row carries no chevron. Every chevroned row in the sheet navigates somewhere; this row acts in place. The trailing slot carries the up-to-date answer when it lands, and the label swaps to it.
- 2026-10-26: an available update follows the What''s New/Help pattern: dismiss the settings sheet, then 150 ms later flip `popupUpdateEnabledAtom`, so the shared modal never sits behind the bottom sheet.
- 2026-10-26: no "checking" transient state. The ticket names the up-to-date answer as the only new surface; the fetch is bounded at ten seconds and Play draws its own progress.
- 2026-10-26: iOS paths that never compare versions (empty store results, unreadable installed version) answer nothing inline. No comparison ran, so no claim of currency.

## Files

- `device/updates.ts`: `startNativeUpdate` result shape; `checkForUpdates` manual option and result type.
- `app/index.tsx`: the automatic call reads `.modal`; no other change.
- `components/sheets/screens/Settings.tsx`: the Other card row, its handler, the inline answer.
- `shared/i18n/en.ts`, `ar.ts`, `so.ts`, `hi.ts`, `ms.ts`, `th.ts`: `settings.checkUpdates` and `settings.upToDate`.
- `shared/i18n/catalog-lock.json`: re-taken with `yarn i18n:lock`, because the English catalog changes.
- `device/__tests__/updates.test.ts`: result-shape and manual-mode tests.
- `__tests__/app/index.test.tsx`: the `checkForUpdates` mock and its resolved values move to the result shape.
- `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/Settings.test.tsx`: the row''s suite.

## Design

One flow, two entry points. `checkForUpdates` keeps its single body; `manual` only widens the throttle gate. The truth table:

| case | modal | upToDate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| throttle refuses (automatic alone) | false | false |
| iOS: store version newer | true | false |
| iOS: comparison ran, not newer | false | true |
| iOS: fetch failed, or nothing to compare | false | false |
| Android: Play answered, no update | false | true |
| Android: Play answered with update (flexible flow started) | false | false |
| Android: Play rejected the check | false | false |

The stamp writes exactly as today: success stamps now, failure stamps an hour back, the throttle-refused automatic call stamps nothing. The automatic launch call in `app/index.tsx` passes no option and reads `.modal`.

The Other card row: a Pressable styled `whatsNewButton` like its siblings, check glyph badge, label `t(''settings.checkUpdates'')`. On press: Medium haptic, then `checkForUpdates({ manual: true })`. A `modal` result dismisses the settings sheet and 150 ms later sets `popupUpdateEnabledAtom` true, which is the same `ModalUpdate` path the launch check uses (it renders in `Index`, gated by `chromeDeferred` and the What''s New/Help exclusivity the modal already carries). An `upToDate` result swaps the label to `t(''settings.upToDate'')` and hides the chevron slot; the row keeps working, so a further tap re-checks and an honest failure resets the label to resting. Any other result changes nothing.

Alternatives rejected: re-showing the update modal for the up-to-date case (the modal has no copy for it, and inventing modal copy widens the surface beyond the ruling); a per-button throttle (owner ruled none); hiding the button on Android (the Play flow is the same single flow, and Android answers inline when Play reports current).

## Steps

1. Step 1: the manual mode and result shape in `device/updates.ts` (2 points). Tests first in `device/__tests__/updates.test.ts`: manual skips the throttle read, manual still stamps success and failure, the automatic throttle tests keep passing against the result shape, `startNativeUpdate` reports availability. Then `app/index.tsx` reads `.modal` and `__tests__/app/index.test.tsx` mocks move to the result shape. One commit.
2. Step 2: the copy in all six catalogs and the lock re-taken (2 points). `settings.checkUpdates` and `settings.upToDate` in en/ar/so/hi/ms/th, `yarn i18n:lock` run, `catalogGates` and `catalogLock` suites green. One commit.
3. Step 3: the Other card row and its suite (2 points). `components/sheets/screens/Settings.tsx` row, handler, inline answer; `Settings.test.tsx` gains the row''s coverage with `@/device/updates` mocked. One commit.

## Risks

- The result-shape change breaks any caller still reading a boolean; the blast radius is two call sites (app/index.tsx, the new row) and three suites, all named above.
- `Settings.tsx` importing `@/device/updates` pulls `expo-in-app-updates` into every suite that renders the sheet. The package resolves from node_modules and only touches native code when called; if a suite still trips, that suite mocks `@/device/updates` the way `app/index.test.tsx` already does.
- The 150 ms modal delay on a fast answer: the delay lands after the network answer, so the sheet is long dismissed; the same 150 ms the What''s New and Help rows already trust.
- A tap during an in-flight check starts a second check; last write wins, and both writes are the same honest value. Owner ruled no throttle.

## Proof

- `yarn jest device/__tests__/updates.test.ts` covers the truth table above, manual and automatic.
- `yarn jest components/sheets/screens/__tests__/Settings.test.tsx` covers: the row renders in the Other card; a press calls `checkForUpdates({ manual: true })`; a modal result closes the sheet and flips `popupUpdateEnabledAtom`; an up-to-date result answers inline; a silent result leaves the row resting.
- `yarn jest __tests__/app/index.test.tsx` keeps every update-prompt test green, proving the automatic path unchanged.
- `git diff origin/uat -- shared/i18n/` shows both keys in all six catalogs and the lock file.
- `yarn validate` green, coverage over every touched line.
